  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature change denoted as Delta T, appearing in the formula for length change alongside normal force and tensile stiffness.&lt;SEP&gt;The temperature change ΔT used in Hooke's model contributing to thermal strain&lt;SEP&gt;A temperature change that leads only to strains (Dehnungen) in an isotropic material without causing shear strains (Gleitungen)&lt;SEP&gt;The German term for temperature changes, which the 3D Hooke's Model accounts for.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359</data>
