  <data key="d2">Graphical representation of the relationship between stress and strain from tension or compression tests&lt;SEP&gt;Diagram (Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm) constructed using stress and strain data, requiring the stress definition as a prerequisite&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm, a diagram constructed using the strain definition that distinguishes elastic recovery from permanent plastic strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Diagrams resulting from tensile and compressive tests that visually represent the experimentally derived relationship between stress and strain for a material.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram illustrating the mechanical behavior of a ductile material, plotting stress ($\sigma$) against strain ($\varepsilon$) during a tensile test.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram used in materials science and structural mechanics to illustrate the behavior of a material under load.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89b8532cdf159a4bfe5be48dea8b78e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763b254f857bc066044052010175b2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d89277cf2e87034384489ad8dc567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a8a17ee36ec3a25041cb22c3b85cd5</data>
