<node id="Normal Stress">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Normal Stress, also known by its German equivalent Normalspannung, is a fundamental mechanical concept originally formalized by Cauchy. It represents the intensity of internal forces, or applied stress, acting perpendicularly to a specified surface, material's cross-section, sectional plane, or the faces of an infinitesimal material element. It induces axial and transverse strains and is typically introduced in foundational mechanics coursework to provide the necessary basis for structural analysis and the calculation of mechanical strain. As a component resulting from the decomposition of the stress vector, it is mathematically expressed as σ_N = t·n.

Normal Stress is denoted by the Greek letter sigma (σ) and is measured in Pascals (Pa or N/m²), or megapascals (MPa). It comprises the direct stress components located on the main diagonal of the symmetric 3x3 stress tensor (σ_xx, σ_yy, and σ_zz), which are often simplified to σ_x, σ_y, and σ_z. Serving as the uniaxial stress input to the constitutive equation, it is notably featured in Hooke's constitutive law, where strain is expressed as ε = σ/E × (1 + ν). 

Mathematically, Normal Stress is calculated by dividing the normal force by the cross-sectional area, generally defined by the equation σ = N/A = F/A. When analyzing variations along an object's length, it is specifically expressed as σ(x) = N(x)/A(x), with values varying by partial derivatives across infinitesimal distances. Positive values denote tensile stress (where the material is stretched or pulled apart, often indicated by outward-pointing arrows on positive faces), while negative values signify compressive stress (where the material is squeezed or pushed together). In practical engineering, it is crucial for evaluating stress distributions in straight bars, uniaxially loaded members, and inclined planes, such as calculating an unknown resultant on an inclined hypotenuse face or analyzing specific problem values like σ_x = 50 MPa and σ_y = -20 MPa. In a pure shear stress state, the normal stress components are equal to zero.

Normal Stress is highly involved in coordinate transformation equations, such as those transforming from an x,y to an η,ξ-system, which are derived using trigonometric identities. In graphical analysis, it is represented by the horizontal axis (sigma, σ) in the Cartesian coordinate system of the Mohr's Circle diagram, with principal stresses labeled as +σ and -σ. Evaluated in the principal axes system within continuum mechanics, its extremal values occur in the principal directions, eventually becoming the principal stresses. This principal angle orientation is found when the derivative of the stress component (σξ) with respect to the cutting angle (φ) is set to zero. Furthermore, Normal Stress acting perpendicular to a plane does not vanish at the planes of maximum or extremal shear stress, where it is mathematically given by the equation σ_n = (σ_1 + σ_2)/2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b47064af1c6b2b2b7fb34a9c6b98111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ec7d98bfb03bb42a21ae886e54257cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f7107d9e481e8d7b78079a1c4ff9229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c0da2a284b623237194f0ea10b2b73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fed5dfab36680bc0a576b0ed9cc7e5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84aaf5f754cbb16f87120d0c3bf0cd2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6513413e0a80f005888472d94d385e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011c3fc433230965d7a734e4052f7689&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36eb7e02adf94546ad8999d1636f68fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b2a42c115ed62e72e715daa89e2370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-271a171e393b79c95418cb0645e75d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef86ae323cfba68764c2acb2d46785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74378ee7045b50cecf2c625c47685477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7876e6fbf1af5b17253567ec9af4cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-765ad24fd0f91713e3dc722570316ee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98ff466f481e3ef48f03b583574686cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2662124ebaa998fdaa13ffecb3add380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60e545266c1919041c313cfba39a94c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb64a0edb671186691ad9f74cd07ae9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2839b8d3cca96c984fc98ff0599ca3a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012508b359d5f14b7a687dd269f97c12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ffd7059b21365543021b6e1a5ac8087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8be23ae96862171a1f9cb78cb1cfcb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6589bf554e5066ac0fa2960ba8d673c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3553477d678ccfb56c56a99c6a713a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cae0fdb4f5af9a553af5e5ec7a633b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a7d19da473048f7577c45363a2702e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edcede9e6d28ea1431d1d8fe530b301d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d97fb385691a70a5c314b2a77a107e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b3409eb9a461816c78110bf52f37f07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadc704f7f5e7980d43e7d870873727e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f35adb2f34cbe81a9755002339ad40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f29928f565c2e69cfd84b7a3af24ffe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b18872f44af51f12eed1b7bb9c974c8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a03cb4a8bcb2904e74a15376b18fddec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5deab09d1c9d30fa6463bb3156b4278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd7867c7c2376ea56c7780cb73e5ec8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963728870ca7c1f5d880eae3e1e47f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4640da85a6d88df2121f23eab1d68369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16cb12dda8d30577bdf35b6755d86117</data>
