  <data key="d2">Technical stress, defined as internal force per cross-sectional area, with units of N/mm^2 or MPa.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress; a fundamental technical topic representing internal forces within structural bars, depicted as a foundational pillar of Chapter 10.&lt;SEP&gt;The German term for stress, representing a primary topic covered in the surrounding content of the document.&lt;SEP&gt;The German word for stress, mentioned in the document context discussing mechanical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress, covered in section 10.1, discussing normal stress in a conical compression member.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress (σ), calculated from the force measured by the load cell during material testing, representing internal force per unit area.</data>
