<node id="Zug- bzw. Druckversuch">
  <data key="d0">Zug- bzw. Druckversuch</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An experimental test (tensile or compressive test) used to determine material models by stretching or compressing a sample bar.&lt;SEP&gt;A tensile or compression test performed using a universal testing machine configuration to determine material properties such as Young's modulus and yield point.&lt;SEP&gt;German term for 'Tensile/compressive testing,' a testing method for determining material properties under tensile or compressive loading.&lt;SEP&gt;An experimental methodology for testing tension or compression discussed in the source material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb8c329536d2e721390485300fec34e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b35bef5073db0c5a31b6dd2e83c0ddb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm">
  <data key="d0">Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A diagrammatic representation used to plot and analyze the relationship between stress and strain obtained from material tests.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress-strain diagram where calculated stress and strain values are plotted to determine material properties including Young's modulus, proportional limit, and yield point.&lt;SEP&gt;German term for 'Stress-strain diagram,' a graphical representation showing the relationship between stress and strain in material science and mechanics.&lt;SEP&gt;A graphical representation of stress-strain diagrams attributed to the academic material.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress-strain diagram discussed in the educational material sourced from Technische Mechanik 2, illustrating elastic and plastic deformation behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress-strain diagram from which the stress or strain at failure of a bar under tensile load can be determined</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb8c329536d2e721390485300fec34e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b35bef5073db0c5a31b6dd2e83c0ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3118530638f20d2b532ee5ac5df3f9a0&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784964350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Spannungs-Dehnungs-Diagramm</data>
</node>
<node id="Knicken">
  <data key="d0">Knicken</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A failure mode (buckling) that can occur in slender bars under compressive loading before the stress reaches an impermissible level.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784894368</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zug Und Druck In Stäben">
  <data key="d0">Zug Und Druck In Stäben</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Chapter 10 of the course material, focusing on the mechanical behavior of bars subjected to tension and compression.&lt;SEP&gt;Chapter 10 titled 'Tension and Compression in Bars' within the lecture material 'Mechanik in der Werkstofftechnik II: Elastostatik', covering topics related to tension and compression in structural bars.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-424242c0995ba02f22fe1c1864ca5f4b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dae0b4038721550e833d3e9407ccd22</data>
