<node id="Generalized Hooke's Law (Tensorial Constitutive Equation for Linear Elasticity) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Generalized Hooke's Law (Tensorial Constitutive Equation for Linear Elasticity) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Tensorial form of Hooke's Law σ = E·ε, the constitutive model defining linear-elastic material behavior by linearly mapping the strain tensor to the stress tensor via the fourth-rank elasticity tensor. Central to Section 10.3 on material laws, it underpins the three-equation framework (equilibrium, kinematics, constitutive law) for structural analysis and reduces to the scalar form σ = E·ε for the uniaxial rod element in Section 10.4.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a093ad0a488172322e66eed43c540981</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784895160</data>
</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law for Linear-Elastic Uniaxial Loading (Inverse Form) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law for Linear-Elastic Uniaxial Loading (Inverse Form) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation expresses Hooke's Law in inverse form, relating strain ε to stress σ through Young's modulus E. It is valid within the linear-elastic regime (σ ≤ σ_p) and constitutes the constitutive material model (Stoffgesetz) for analyzing single rod structures under axial loading, forming one of three fundamental equation systems in structural mechanics analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784895160</data>
</node>
<node id="Stress-Strain Diagram illustrating Elastic-Plastic Material Behavior (image)">
  <data key="d0">Stress-Strain Diagram illustrating Elastic-Plastic Material Behavior (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This image is a stress-strain diagram (σ-ε Diagram) that visualizes the results of a tensile test (Zugversuch). It depicts the relationship between stress and strain, highlighting the linear-elastic region (Hooke's Law), the yield point (σ_F), and the plastic deformation region. Crucially, it shows the unloading path ('Entlastung') resulting in permanent plastic strain (ε_pl) and contrasts engineering stress (σ = F/A) with true stress (σ_w = F/A_w). This serves as a graphical representation of the 'Stoffgesetz' (material law) concepts discussed in the accompanying text regarding material modeling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-73a8a17ee36ec3a25041cb22c3b85cd5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784895160</data>
</node>
