<node id="Hooke's Law">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hooke's Law is a fundamental principle of physics and linear elasticity that serves as a foundational constitutive law or material model. Also known as the Law of Elasticity, "Elastizitätsgesetz," or "Hooksches Modell," it describes the relationship between stress and strain in homogeneous, isotropic elastic materials. The law establishes a linear relationship where normal stress is directly proportional to normal strain via a proportionality constant known as Young's modulus or the elastic modulus (E). This uniaxial relationship is mathematically expressed as σ = E · ε or inversely as ε = σ / E. Hooke's Law applies strictly within the linear-elastic regime—the initial elastic region of the stress-strain diagram where stress does not exceed the proportional limit—and relies on the assumption of small deformations.

In engineering and structural mechanics, Hooke's Law is extensively used for elastic deformation calculations in stress analysis. For slender structural members and prismatic bars under uniaxial tension and compression, it is used to calculate axial deformation by relating the change in length to internal axial force, initial length, and axial rigidity (EA), expressed as ΔL = FL / EA or Δl = Sl / EA. As a critical framework for solving complex structural problems, including statically indeterminate systems, it is integrated with equilibrium and kinematic compatibility conditions to relate bar forces to elongations. This combination allows engineers to determine axial force distributions, principal normal strains, and displacements, ultimately producing the governing ordinary differential equation for displacement.

Beyond normal stress, Hooke's Law is generalized for plane stress conditions, biaxial stress, and three-dimensional (3D) linearly elastic materials. It articulates linear relationships for shear components, relating shear stress (τ) and shear strain (γ) via the shear modulus (G) as τ = Gγ. Under biaxial or plane stress conditions, it determines normal strain using the equation ε = σ(1+ν)/E, where ν represents Poisson's ratio. The generalized 3D model relates the stress and strain tensors and holds in any arbitrary Cartesian coordinate system sharing the same principal directions as the stress tensor. Furthermore, this linear elastic assumption yields the 1/2 coefficient in the strain energy equation—representing the area under the linear stress-strain curve—and its parameters (E and ν) are relied upon by hydrostatic strain energy density equations. The law is also extended to model thermoelasticity, acting as a material model that incorporates thermal expansion terms to describe the relationship between stress and strain.

As a vital theoretical framework in engineering education and technical literature, Hooke's Law is comprehensively addressed in textbooks such as "Technische Mechanik 2." Specifically, it is detailed in Section 12.2 (titled Elastizitätsgesetz) and introduced on page 10, while the generalized constitutive equation relating stress and strain tensors is formally presented on page 17. The foundational physical model, which includes the derivation of the relationship between modulus of elasticity and shear modulus and is supported by Section 11.4 for thermoelasticity, utilizes critical algebraic steps like the Tangent Equation within its broader mathematical framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6fc1a89775e67ed1be0c24a11e1773f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe61c354100bb43a98ebc62d57cf28c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7cfa532d0224ec6532c6354495df59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc78afbb216db05f32ee167a8643581f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1fe24f4724db937ef65aa2cd2c2fab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23f9a8f34af690fb6d5cb0ea12f409a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edab2d4bca40b7e16cfc072b04cebe0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89b8532cdf159a4bfe5be48dea8b78e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cd2fb9e592523746e131ec4c914481&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-763b254f857bc066044052010175b2b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad3e7d061ebaf26776716772bd7daeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d89277cf2e87034384489ad8dc567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783555881f4ab73d4d04ea548b9fae1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fed5dfab36680bc0a576b0ed9cc7e5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151ad67dcab298d7226da28fe7afb340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f0665902c9df9b5ec4573eb02f74a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6d370949ced2e82caca9443dede62a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a7f9fd51bacb1b5261081565de649fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73a8a17ee36ec3a25041cb22c3b85cd5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab59a548a45f0f75802088fe89a02c30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3118530638f20d2b532ee5ac5df3f9a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b12d2d988ba8fdb9