<node id="Tensile Stiffness">
  <data key="d0">Tensile Stiffness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A compound material-geometric parameter representing the resistance of the bar to axial deformation, calculated as Young's Modulus multiplied by cross-sectional area.&lt;SEP&gt;The product EA (Dehnsteifigkeit), a key parameter in structural analysis representing resistance to axial deformation&lt;SEP&gt;The product EA representing resistance to axial deformation, shared equally by both bars in the system</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe61c354100bb43a98ebc62d57cf28c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de</data>
