  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal force at position x along the bar, used as a component in the stress equation σ(x) = N(x) / A(x)&lt;SEP&gt;The internal normal force within a rod element, related to distributed loads through the equilibrium condition.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal axial force within a structural member, which equals zero when Axial Force F is zero.&lt;SEP&gt;An internal force quantity whose determination is a key step in bar analysis, discussed within Section 10.4 Einzelstab.</data>
