<node id="Stress Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Stress Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented by σ = N/A, the distribution of stress determined using the internal normal force N divided by the cross-sectional area A, fundamental to axially-loaded structural members.&lt;SEP&gt;The spread of internal forces (σ = N/A) across a cross-section, which equals zero when normal force is zero.&lt;SEP&gt;The spatial distribution of internal stresses within a structural element, to which self-weight contributes significantly in applications like cables and tensile elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The distribution of stress in cross-sections, covered in the surrounding content discussing Section 11.1 on stress vectors and stress tensors.</data>
