<node id="Young's Modulus">
  <data key="d0">Young's Modulus</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Young's Modulus, also widely known as the modulus of elasticity, E-Modul, or Elastizitätsmodul, is a fundamental mechanical and scalar material property that measures the stiffness of a solid, isotropic elastic material. Universally denoted by the variable $E$, it characterizes a material's resistance to elastic deformation, specifically defining its tensile or compressive stiffness under axial loading. As a material-specific proportionality constant, it represents the direct ratio of mechanical stress to strain within the linear-elastic deformation range.

In material science and structural mechanics, Young's Modulus serves as a foundational constant in Hooke's Law and linear-elastic constitutive relations. It dictates how a structure or component resists deformation when subjected to an applied load by acting as an inverse scaling factor between mechanical stress and strain. This relationship is prominently featured in the mechanical strain equation ($\varepsilon = \sigma/E$), where it serves as the denominator in the compliance factor (1/E) to calculate mechanical strain. Additionally, $E$ is a crucial parameter used in the compliance matrix to calculate axial strain and is utilized to derive principal strains from principal stresses.

Beyond basic stress-strain relationships, Young's Modulus is an essential parameter utilized across various governing equations for axial displacement and deformation. For structural components such as uniaxial bar elements and rods, $E$ is applied to calculate axial rigidity (EA), internal normal forces, the elongation of bar segments, and elastic shortenings. It appears explicitly in the mechanical elongation terms of compatibility equations, the axial force equation, constitutive equations for internal energy calculations, and the governing differential equations for structural materials. In these analytical contexts, it is consistently treated as an assumed constant that accurately represents the elastic stiffness of the material.

Young's Modulus is mathematically related to other fundamental material properties, most notably the Shear Modulus and Poisson's ratio, allowing for comprehensive derivations of material behavior. It is measured in units of pressure or stress, such as Pascals [Pa] or Newtons per square meter (N/m²) and Newtons per square millimeter (N/mm²). For practical engineering applications, these measurements are frequently scaled to megapascals (MPa).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe61c354100bb43a98ebc62d57cf28c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17078647094adcc12a6785492579bc48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920d899bb09d20ddc75b79ec193db2e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-051ef03c9d8a42ed1589c14c82007f4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-055d89277cf2e87034384489ad8dc567&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783555881f4ab73d4d04ea548b9fae1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a093ad0a488172322e66eed43c540981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f547ed992922c6608475aa607ecc95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f6cb959dc0f4ce6e1902a94dcb7d12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b37ac6d222ba4898f7b2f8f457e77e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbe1099c718b59c4f95b165b71f72ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5deab09d1c9d30fa6463bb3156b4278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2fbc89309c5fa28f062356d8fd0dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f286bbba14a03f81052794f20378e5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f0f77e6766d722b567e55f8b17701c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-529957e83da207a93efc376cc085ff93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4b387a69caef33cbbc0d01cd946a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963728870ca7c1f5d880eae3e1e47f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2929c1e9ff7a4d28ae04567e99b7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4640da85a6d88df2121f23eab1d68369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804dc5da5931340fcffd232bf52ac41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f3dbcdc7efa91f1ffd56d0596ff25b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95513f4440188d0181ac3f745cc0cfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650f3440dee3d2c3acd18a9d3ea4f7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718443b278fc05d9b29615dd32329bd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-665c0dff808ce919d3762159ff91d81a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c347d0d02f605dcaeeba6088d212ddc8</data>
