<node id="Change In Length">
  <data key="d0">Change In Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted by Δl, the absolute change in length of a bar element (Stabelement) under mechanical loading.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted by Δl, it represents the change in length (elongation or contraction) of a structural member&lt;SEP&gt;The elongation or deformation ($\Delta l_i$) of each bar, determined by applying Hooke's Law to relate internal force, initial length, and axial rigidity&lt;SEP&gt;The difference between the new length and the original length of a segment, isolated as the product of the partial derivative of displacement and the original infinitesimal length.&lt;SEP&gt;The elongation or deformation of a material element, calculated as the product of normal strain and original length.&lt;SEP&gt;The change in length of the material element after deformation, denoted by $\Delta l$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-738c698a563cc3405e3c1de5794fa318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f286bbba14a03f81052794f20378e5cc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
