<node id="Coefficient Of Linear Thermal Expansion">
  <data key="d0">Coefficient Of Linear Thermal Expansion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The material property (α_T) used to calculate thermal strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted as α_T, a material-specific scalar quantity with units [1/K] that determines how much a material expands per unit of temperature change&lt;SEP&gt;The material property alpha_T that determines the thermal strain component for a given temperature change.&lt;SEP&gt;A material property denoted as αT that characterizes the free thermal expansion of the heated rod segment per unit temperature change.&lt;SEP&gt;A material property ($\alpha_T$) used to calculate the thermal strain of a solid based on temperature changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f197243eeecfe8da4e162edc85af353&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95513f4440188d0181ac3f745cc0cfe1</data>
