<node id="Original Length">
  <data key="d0">Original Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted as l, representing the initial length of the bar before deformation, used as the denominator in the engineering strain ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted as l, the initial length of a prismatic bar measured in meters [m]&lt;SEP&gt;The initial length of the infinitesimal line element, denoted as dy.&lt;SEP&gt;The initial, undeformed length of a material element.&lt;SEP&gt;The initial length of the material element before deformation, denoted by $l$.&lt;SEP&gt;The undeformed, initial length of a line segment, represented by the variable l.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a371746d42ee15c97ccf2f983b9237ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2deea6eaa78cd0a482432f78f4310b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f286bbba14a03f81052794f20378e5cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4</data>
