</node>
<node id="10.1 Spannung">
  <data key="d0">10.1 Spannung</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The first technical content section located on page 2, covering the topic of stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 10.1 within Chapter 10, introducing fundamental concepts of Stress analysis in bars, including the definition of the bar axis, the relationship between external load and internal forces, normal stress, and sign conventions for tensile and compressive stress.&lt;SEP&gt;A numbered section header (10.1 Stress) from a German-language technical mechanics or strength of materials document, serving as the organizational anchor for mechanical stress theory. It connects theoretical stress definitions to practical engineering design considerations including cross-section dimensioning and design constraints.</data>
