</node>
<node id="Internal Forces">
  <data key="d0">Internal Forces</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Forces within a structural element that are determined using the section method, as outlined in the chapter's learning objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces that act within a structural member, which are analyzed using an imaginary transverse cut plane.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces generated within a structural element to maintain equilibrium against external loads.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces generated internally within a structural element in response to external loads, discussed within Section 10.1 Spannung.&lt;SEP&gt;The internal forces within bars '1' and '2' that need to be determined in the example problem.&lt;SEP&gt;Forces distributed across a defined section of a solid object that result from the application of external loads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b47064af1c6b2b2b7fb34a9c6b98111d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed3c14262e18f66ed415c1b72900af48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a81d55be35cb5a2d86799183a37d1295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dae0b4038721550e833d3e9407ccd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae0b855416df86edb6af7ac8d0407fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2616f80e6ffe22a7bb18ebfbbc1b015a</data>
