</node>
<node id="Delta l_1">
  <data key="d0">Delta l_1</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A horizontal segment representing the calculated axial elongation of bar 1, starting from the vertical projection of Point C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6681170cb4ff75b4d310df8342f3aad9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Delta l_2">
  <data key="d0">Delta l_2</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A slanted segment representing the calculated axial elongation of bar 2, extending from Point C along the axis of line 2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6681170cb4ff75b4d310df8342f3aad9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Displacement Assumption">
  <data key="d0">Small Displacement Assumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theoretical principle mentioned in Section 10.5 that is visually demonstrated by the diagram's displacement analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;An analytical assumption required for the validity of linearizing circular arcs using tangent approximations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6681170cb4ff75b4d310df8342f3aad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad1fe24f4724db937ef65aa2cd2c2fab</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
