<node id="Free-Body Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Free-Body Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A technical diagram depicting a vertical structural element with labeled forces, coordinate variables, and boundaries illustrating static equilibrium.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical schematic visual representation displaying the equilibrium of forces at node C, using a clear style common in engineering textbooks&lt;SEP&gt;The upper portion of the technical image illustrating the equilibrium of forces at node C with red force vectors&lt;SEP&gt;The functional role of the technical schematic diagram, used to facilitate the derivation of equilibrium conditions for the pressure vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagram showing all stresses and body forces acting on the isolated infinitesimal element, used to derive the governing equilibrium equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5b9805139d42f6eef23df04f62f07811&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c113cfbbfa4f8142d716b5538931026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ec6927ab0bb507f573af8049b45847&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36eb7e02adf94546ad8999d1636f68fa</data>
