</node>
<node id="Statically Determinate">
  <data key="d0">Statically Determinate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A problem-solving methodology category for single bar scenarios where internal forces and reactions can be determined solely from equilibrium equations, referred to as "statisch bestimmte" in German.&lt;SEP&gt;Classification of the governing ODE problem indicating that internal forces can be determined from equilibrium alone without additional compatibility equations&lt;SEP&gt;A structural property where internal forces and constants can be determined solely by static equilibrium equations.&lt;SEP&gt;A classification of the hanging rod problem indicating that support reactions can be determined from equilibrium equations alone without requiring compatibility conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e31c68f0ed98d537493847b61aa6024c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920d899bb09d20ddc75b79ec193db2e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Indeterminate">
  <data key="d0">Statically Indeterminate</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A problem-solving methodology category for single bar scenarios requiring additional compatibility equations beyond equilibrium, referred to as "statisch unbestimmte" in German.&lt;SEP&gt;A structural property requiring geometric compatibility equations in addition to equilibrium to solve for constants.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e31c68f0ed98d537493847b61aa6024c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920d899bb09d20ddc75b79ec193db2e5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896984</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Differential Equations">
  <data key="d0">Differential Equations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The governing differential equations that describe the mechanical behavior of axially loaded single bar systems, detailed within the Einzelstab section.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical equations formulated in the document to describe bar displacement under various loads.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e31c68f0ed98d537493847b61aa6024c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcf46285e4f22dfa1724a1fa4063d3f</data>
