<node id="Engineering Mechanics">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Mechanics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Engineering Mechanics is a broad scientific discipline and academic field concerned with the state of rest or motion of physical bodies when subjected to the action of forces. As a comprehensive theoretical framework, it encompasses the study of mechanical equations, physical principles, and structural analysis. The discipline broadly integrates major sub-fields such as continuum mechanics, kinematics, and the strength of materials (*Festigkeitslehre*), the latter of which specifically focuses on material laws and in-depth stress analysis.

Within Engineering Mechanics, fundamental structural components like the *Einzelstab* (single bar or rod) serve as essential elements for detailed discussions on mechanical properties, including tensile stiffness and the analysis of statically determinate bar systems. The field is deeply concerned with the behavior of physical bodies under stress, requiring the determination of critical loading directions. Practical and theoretical applications within this discipline involve the use of principal stress analysis in structural design and failure theories, as well as graphical stress transformations such as Mohr's Circle.

As a foundational academic subject, Engineering Mechanics is heavily codified in scholarly documents and established standard literature. Notably, the textbook *Technische Mechanik 2* is widely recognized as an authoritative and standard work within this field. This text, along with other cited literature, serves to demonstrate the fundamental equations, standard mechanical principles, and analytical diagrams that comprise the core of the Engineering Mechanics curriculum.&lt;SEP&gt;The academic discipline encompassing the topics discussed in the document and the referenced textbook.&lt;SEP&gt;A field of engineering that encompasses spatial stress states and equivalent stress calculations.&lt;SEP&gt;A field of study, also known as Technische Mechanik, focusing on strength hypotheses and stress transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad field of study whose complex concepts are discussed in the educational material and the textbook.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-71dad38576055c6e013578d06064a913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e31c68f0ed98d537493847b61aa6024c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5281233f3c19ef2742208835bb41bd76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10de6334f28b94ed6f4ea9af906f66c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ad3e7d061ebaf26776716772bd7daeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd72d98943d7e0523296223aa7032d98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151ad67dcab298d7226da28fe7afb340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7401c00a8316a2124dcb1cf703b5f16d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5bec24cc4d96b66479607814f58f26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6ea2012f708d083bcf1f8357bfab292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-765ad24fd0f91713e3dc722570316ee2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eaae8681c23616569341d164404cba8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea236c2c090948676eebcd4986bd6df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0139ebf1ce9f9e12ac7fedf1b939a2f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3553477d678ccfb56c56a99c6a713a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-269e2be218f17e48feb7ecb2c0ddf3f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00185afb9a5d259c31643f50551104c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b562c6cf8ea640066c4829c2dbc8a288&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68f46a2f336e00af32ab51674b243da4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af524c4a39d0752767ee95f685a1fb6b</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
