<node id="Technical Engineering Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Technical Engineering Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">This technical engineering diagram illustrates the distribution of normal stress in a straight bar subjected to axial tensile forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The visual representation illustrating the statically determinate two-bar truss system.&lt;SEP&gt;An image illustrating a two-dimensional stress state on a material element, characterized by clean vector lines and high-contrast colors typical of academic textbooks.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical engineering diagram illustrating the stress state within a thin-walled cylindrical pressure vessel (Dünnwandiger Kessel), divided into four distinct panels labeled a, b, c, and d, using grey shading for solid vessel components, bright red for vector quantities such as pressure and stress, and black typography for mathematical symbols and dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical diagram illustrating the deformation of a material element under a specific state of biaxial stress.</data>
