</node>
<node id="Material Science">
  <data key="d0">Material Science</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A field of study where the strain equation is used to determine material limits such as yield strain.&lt;SEP&gt;A field of science that is the thematic context of the surrounding lecture content.&lt;SEP&gt;A scientific field that uses derived strain quantities to predict material failure.&lt;SEP&gt;A field concerned with the properties and behavior of materials, for which strain transformation theory provides a theoretical foundation.&lt;SEP&gt;Field in which the shear strain equation is used for predicting deformation patterns and material behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;A branch of science that, alongside continuum mechanics, serves as an application domain for this equation, specifically concerning the theory of plasticity and failure analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A field of study related to the von Mises yield criterion and material strength hypotheses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86444d41dc2e58cbf77ceb58838e96c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-154d19114c3f301c7c7a909d141ce692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d00610e182d45a94eb2e712fcaa111a3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statics">
  <data key="d0">Statics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The study of internal normal force and stress, from which the study transitions to kinematics via the strain equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
