</node>
<node id="Constitutive Laws">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Laws</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Stress-strain relationships that fully describe elastic body behavior, for which the strain equation lays the foundation.&lt;SEP&gt;Laws (Stoffgesetze) that phenomenologically connect strains to stresses, formulated based on the geometric foundation of the kinematic relationship&lt;SEP&gt;Material models (Stoffgesetze) describing the physical relationship between stress and strain, which are material-dependent.&lt;SEP&gt;A topic within elastostatics typically covered in the textbook Technische Mechanik 2.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical laws formulated using the analytical bridge between the kinematic description of deformation and the strain state.&lt;SEP&gt;Physical laws (Elastizitätsgesetz) that relate strains to stresses through specific material parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;A topic covered within Chapter 12 of the textbook.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7191762e3c837260ad5bf3f1bc50f25a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f44965262ad3a19924f66261ac5694c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-266b49cf12495861b99ca9dc21275e0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f4c091fae29a6bd21771fd542eb9801</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinetics">
  <data key="d0">Kinetics</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The branch of mechanics dealing with applied forces, which result in geometric changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9650cbfdac35d71c763ff0baacdc1c9c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
