  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement U(x)">
  <data key="d0">Displacement U(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A kinematic quantity introduced in the Kinematik section to describe deformation geometry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23f9a8f34af690fb6d5cb0ea12f409a1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strain Ε">
  <data key="d0">Strain Ε</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A kinematic quantity introduced alongside displacement to describe deformation geometry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-23f9a8f34af690fb6d5cb0ea12f409a1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S₁">
  <data key="d0">S₁</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal axial force (Stabkraft) in bar 1, equal to S₃ by horizontal equilibrium due to symmetric bar configuration with EA₃ = EA₁.&lt;SEP&gt;Axial force in bar 1 of the three-bar truss system, equal to S₃ due to geometric and material symmetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S₃">
  <data key="d0">S₃</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal axial force (Stabkraft) in bar 3, equal to S₁ by horizontal equilibrium due to symmetric bar configuration with EA₃ = EA₁.&lt;SEP&gt;Axial force in bar 3 of the three-bar truss system, equal to S₁ due to geometric and material symmetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="S₂">
  <data key="d0">S₂</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal axial force in bar 2 of the three-bar structural system, determined via compatibility condition and Hooke's law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Alpha (α)">
  <data key="d0">Alpha (α)</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The angle from the vertical axis at which bars 1 and 3 are symmetrically arranged in the three-bar structural system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Equilibrium Condition">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Equilibrium Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The condition B - C = 0 confirming that both support reactions are identical in magnitude.&lt;SEP&gt;The summation of horizontal force components (ΣH = 0) at node K, yielding S₁ = S₃ due to the symmetric configuration of bars 1 and 3.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Equilibrium Equation">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Equilibrium Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation S₁cosα + S₂ + S₃cosα - F = 0 governing vertical force balance, which combined with S₁ = S₃ leaves only S₂ as the unknown.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compatibility Condition">
  <data key="d0">Compatibility Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A geometric constraint enforced in statically indeterminate structures, such as Δl = 0 for a doubly-clamped rod where both ends are restrained.&lt;SEP&gt;The condition that the total elongation of the bar is zero, meaning the bar is prevented from elongating.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinematic constraint that total elongation must vanish (Δl = Δl₁ + Δl₂ = 0) since both ends of the compound rod are fixed&lt;SEP&gt;The condition that the total elongation of the bar equals zero (Delta l1 + Delta l2 = 0) since both supports are rigid.&lt;SEP&gt;A Verträglichkeitsbedingung ensuring boundary conditions, such as zero displacement at a fixed support, are satisfied.&lt;SEP&gt;The boundary condition requiring the total elongation of the rod to vanish (Δl = Δl1 + Δl2 = 0).&lt;SEP&gt;The kinematic compatibility condition (Δl₁ = Δl₂cosα) that supplements equilibrium equations for solving statically indeterminate bar systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a93c57c2e2028051403eda908d55fe3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Indeterminate Three-Bar System">
  <data key="d0">Statically Indeterminate Three-Bar System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural system where equilibrium alone is insufficient to determine all internal forces, requiring additional kinematic compatibility conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EA₁">
  <data key="d0">EA₁</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The axial rigidity (modulus of elasticity times cross-sectional area) of bar 1, which is equal to EA₃ in the symmetric system.&lt;SEP&gt;Axial rigidity of the inclined bars (bars 1 and 3), defined as Young's modulus E multiplied by cross-sectional area A, with EA₁ equal to EA₃.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9966746921724686a393e234327d9e41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="EA₃">
  <data key="d0">EA₃</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The axial rigidity (modulus of elasticity times cross-sectional area) of bar 3, which is equal to EA₁ in the symmetric system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Horizontal Components">
  <data key="d0">Horizontal Components</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The trigonometric projections of the bar forces (S₁·sinα and S₃·sinα) representing their effect in the horizontal direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d49057dad0c3acc1a3ce1afb3e687a5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Line Load">
  <data key="d0">Line Load</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Constant distributed axial load n = G/l representing the bar's self-weight per unit length&lt;SEP&gt;Denoted as n = G/l (Streckenlast), representing the constant weight per unit length of the rod.&lt;SEP&gt;The constant distributed load n = G/l representing the weight per unit length of the rod.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17078647094adcc12a6785492579bc48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6e4242a538dfbd7e7ae0462ee78fbc7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boundary Value Problem">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Value Problem</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical formulation completed by boundary conditions u(0) = 0 for fixed support and u'(l) = 0 for free end</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-Dimensional Structural Member">
  <data key="d0">One-Dimensional Structural Member</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A rod or bar under distributed axial load, the physical system whose axial displacement field is governed by the ODE E·A·u'' = -n</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bar Length">
  <data key="d0">Bar Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The longitudinal length of the bar, represented by the variable L, used in computing the classical elongation formula.&lt;SEP&gt;Length l of the one-dimensional structural member, appearing in boundary conditions u'(l) = 0, line load definition n = G/l, and elongation Δl = u(l)&lt;SEP&gt;The longitudinal measure of the bar, represented by $l$, used to calculate the distributed load and internal normal force.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement Solution">
