</node>
<node id="Kinematic Compatibility Condition">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Compatibility Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical condition that sets the total axial deformation of a statically indeterminate system to zero, evaluating the boundary condition Δl = Δl1 + Δl2 = 0 for a doubly clamped rod.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Verträglichkeitsbedingung, a geometric requirement that deformations must be consistent with the system's constraints, essential for solving statically indeterminate systems where equilibrium conditions alone are insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;A geometric condition (Δl1 = Δl2 cos α) relating bar elongations, into which material law equations are substituted to solve for unknown forces and displacements</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Bar System">
  <data key="d0">Three-Bar System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural system of three bars (Stäbe) where bars 1 and 3 are symmetrically placed with identical geometric and material properties and carry equal forces&lt;SEP&gt;A structural system consisting of three bars with stiffnesses EA₁, EA₂, and EA₃, loaded at knot K, and classified as singly statically indeterminate.&lt;SEP&gt;A simply statically indeterminate structural system consisting of a middle vertical bar and two inclined bars loaded at a common node.&lt;SEP&gt;A worked example in Section 10.6 involving a system of three bars with axial rigidities EA₁, EA₂, EA₃ = EA₁, whose solution includes substitution into a compatibility equation and determination of bar forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5d7eea8f9e0a901768256832130203b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edab2d4bca40b7e16cfc072b04cebe0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891c97c9b24173fa3943bf0d59b8fa9</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Initial Length">
  <data key="d0">Initial Length</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The original length ($l_i$) of each bar before deformation, used in Hooke's Law equations to calculate the change in length</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fe1aa2ab22c57b58f370cf064cf7ce98</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
