  <data key="d2">A page number element displaying the value '18' located at the bottom of page_idx 13 (zero-indexed) in a German engineering mechanics textbook, positioned at coordinates [29, 907, 43, 927] indicating a standard footer position on the left side.&lt;SEP&gt;A page in the lecture material that established the problem of a three-bar system with bars (Stäbe) of stiffnesses EA₁, EA₂, EA₃, loaded at knot K, classified as singly statically indeterminate.&lt;SEP&gt;A page containing trigonometric identities expressing sin(2φ*) and cos(2φ*) as rational functions of stress components&lt;SEP&gt;Page number 18 of a technical document covering Section 12.2 'Elastizitätsgesetz'.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cc79c4ab764f023bc17eed0dd0b44b48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5d7eea8f9e0a901768256832130203b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359</data>
