<node id="Small Displacements">
  <data key="d0">Small Displacements</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An assumption in the geometric analysis where circular arcs can be approximated by their tangents, used to derive the elongation of the inclined bar.&lt;SEP&gt;Minor movements of neighboring points evaluated in the 1-dimensional case, requiring mathematical formalism via Taylor series expansions for accurate description.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition in mechanics where displacements are sufficiently small to allow linear approximations, analyzed using Taylor series in the lecture material.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d9d584003e02eb55f646636643aaba8</data>
