</node>
<node id="Δl">
  <data key="d0">Δl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable representing the elongation of the bar caused by its weight.&lt;SEP&gt;The total thermal elongation of the bar, resulting from integrating the linear thermal strain ε_T over the bar length&lt;SEP&gt;Change in length, denoted as Längenänderung, of the bar or rod element&lt;SEP&gt;The absolute change in length (elongation or contraction) due to applied stresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-542bf3a4290d267cd5257b52563c594f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ">
  <data key="d0">σ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A variable representing the normal stress within the bar caused by its weight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Greek letter sigma representing normal stress, labeled on the horizontal axis of the coordinate system used in Mohr's Circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903867</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strain-Displacement Equation">
  <data key="d0">Strain-Displacement Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation ε(x) = du/dx = Δl/l representing the fundamental strain-displacement relationship in one-dimensional continuum mechanics, establishing the local strain field as the spatial derivative of the displacement field&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental kinematic relation used for defining the spatial strain tensor components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineering Strain">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The dimensionless ratio of total elongation Δl to original length l, also called technical strain, applicable for homogeneous deformation&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Technische Dehnung, the fundamental definition of strain in one-dimensional continuum mechanics, defined as the ratio of change in length to original reference length, denoted by ε. It is a dimensionless kinematic quantity describing the geometry of deformation.&lt;SEP&gt;A dimensionless measure of deformation representing the ratio of absolute elongation to original length, denoted by the symbol epsilon and referred to as Dehnung.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85da86ad0233986cf40614b65dc61ad2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Small Deformation Hypothesis">
  <data key="d0">Small Deformation Hypothesis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The assumption that |Δl| ≪ l or |ε| ≪ 1, which linearizes the strain measure in the kinematic description of deformation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ae0372192096a8671eab765c6a11a90</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
