  <data key="d0">$x$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A coordinate variable measuring the distance downwards from the top boundary of the depicted segment along the bar.&lt;SEP&gt;A blue axis of the Cartesian coordinate system that lies entirely within the plane of the plate.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e2cb25fd70f2b5f3b6c22629fe461a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="$N(x)$">
  <data key="d0">$N(x)$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal normal force acting within the bar at position $x$, represented by a thick red upward-pointing arrow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="$G^*$">
  <data key="d0">$G^*$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The partial weight of the bar segment located below position $x$, represented by a thick red downward-pointing arrow.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Static Equilibrium Condition">
  <data key="d0">Static Equilibrium Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical state where the internal tensile force balances the cumulative weight of the material suspended below a given point.&lt;SEP&gt;The condition where the sum of forces equals zero in a given direction, mathematically expressed as sum of F_xi equals zero</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hängender Stab unter Eigengewicht">
  <data key="d0">Hängender Stab unter Eigengewicht</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An example scenario of a hanging bar under its own weight discussed in the surrounding text.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="10.4 Einzelstab">
  <data key="d0">10.4 Einzelstab</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A contextual section reference indicating the topic of a single bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="$G$">
  <data key="d0">$G$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The total weight of the bar, appearing in the mathematical expression $G^*= \frac{l-x}{l} G$ used to calculate the partial weight of the bar segment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c2ec62b2ae01b69aeae754d5bb1c9dcb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress (Normalspannung)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The technical normal stress σ(x) at a position x along an axially-loaded bar, representing the average normal stress distributed uniformly over the cross-section, expressed in units of N/mm² or MPa</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Force (Normalkraft)">
  <data key="d0">Normal Force (Normalkraft)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal resultant force N(x) acting perpendicular to the cross-section at position x, obtained via the method of sections by passing a cutting plane through the bar and enforcing equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-sectional Area (Querschnittsfläche)">
  <data key="d0">Cross-sectional Area (Querschnittsfläche)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The area A(x) of the cross-section at position x, which may vary along the bar's longitudinal axis, used as the denominator in the normal stress equation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cauchy's Stress Theory">
  <data key="d0">Cauchy's Stress Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress theory that forms the theoretical foundation for the definition of technical normal stress in axially-loaded bars</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Method of Sections (Schnittverfahren)">
  <data key="d0">Method of Sections (Schnittverfahren)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A procedure for determining internal forces by passing a cutting plane s-s through a structural member and enforcing equilibrium conditions</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-section Dimensioning (Querschnittsbemessung)">
  <data key="d0">Cross-section Dimensioning (Querschnittsbemessung)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The engineering process of determining the minimum required cross-sectional area using the formula A_erf = |N|/σ_zul, ensuring that stress does not exceed an allowable value</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Concentrations (Spannungsspitzen)">
  <data key="d0">Stress Concentrations (Spannungsspitzen)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-uniform stress distributions that occur near bar ends, notches (Kerben), and geometric discontinuities, which cannot be captured by elementary stress theory</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Buckling (Knicken)">
  <data key="d0">Buckling (Knicken)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A failure mode that slender compression members must be checked for, as it may precede stress failure</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tension Member (Zugstab)">
  <data key="d0">Tension Member (Zugstab)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural member subject to axial tension, where N(x) &gt; 0 produces positive tensile stress σ &gt; 0</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compression Member (Druckstab)">
  <data key="d0">Compression Member (Druckstab)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural member subject to axial compression, where N(x) &lt; 0 yields negative compressive stress σ &lt; 0</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axially-Loaded Bar (Stab)">
  <data key="d0">Axially-Loaded Bar (Stab)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural member subjected to axial loading, along which the normal force, cross-sectional area, and normal stress are evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cutting Plane s-s">
  <data key="d0">Cutting Plane s-s</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theoretical plane passed through a structural member, used in the method of sections to expose and calculate internal forces.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Notches (Kerben)">
  <data key="d0">Notches (Kerben)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Geometric discontinuities or features in a structural member where stress concentrations occur and elementary stress theory fails.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Strain">
  <data key="d0">Technical Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A kinematic quantity representing strain, mathematically denoted as epsilon, which is defined under the topic of Dehnung.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40c9b6d63b8c22a4bba35a9a76979235</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stoffgesetz">
  <data key="d0">Stoffgesetz</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Material Law, which describes the behavior of materials under load and relates kinematic measures to force-based measures like stress.&lt;SEP&gt;A material model discussed in preceding sections of the document, preceding the page numbered 12.&lt;SEP&gt;German term for 'Material law,' describing the constitutive relationship between stress and strain in materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40c9b6d63b8c22a4bba35a9a76979235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151ad67dcab298d7226da28fe7afb340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Kinematics Of Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Kinematics Of Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The study of deformation kinematics and kinematic quantities within engineering mechanics, a topic covered in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;The study of the geometry of motion and deformation of physical bodies without considering the forces that cause them.&lt;SEP&gt;An introductory topic setting up the formal treatment of strain tensors and the elasticity law.&lt;SEP&gt;A fundamental concept in continuum mechanics related to the analysis of how deformable bodies change shape.&lt;SEP&gt;The study of deformation motion in continuum mechanics, for which the normal strain ε_x is central and which bridges the kinematic description of surface bodies with the displacement vector field&lt;SEP&gt;Also referred to as Verzerrungszustand, representing the context in which points P and Q are analyzed as neighboring material points in a continuous body.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Verzerrungszustand, a framework studying how small deformations alter the lengths and angles of a material body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40c9b6d63b8c22a4bba35a9a76979235&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a647d5317d835efced8e4c2f0cdae43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d89ad2ee139d73e0b1367cc96d8b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf7262993e514ad26ba97ab4f2a420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a2dbfa0f426be66876905754d3b98be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5b74b4caf274c8a818b5e7d868904b3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998771</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Length L">
  <data key="d0">Length L</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The identical length of both segments of the horizontal bar, denoted by the symbol '$l$'.&lt;SEP&gt;The horizontal distance from the vertical rigid wall to joint C, measured as 'l'.&lt;SEP&gt;The length of the central vertical member and the distance from the support to Node K.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df979c16e8c52bf800fb84c3a4a4bdea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94aa1e1d6b738ff40ac94957c9a7084a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dimension Line">
  <data key="d0">Dimension Line</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A graphical annotation in the diagram indicating the horizontal distance from the wall to joint C.&lt;SEP&gt;A double-headed vertical line indicating the length 'l' of the central vertical member.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94aa1e1d6b738ff40ac94957c9a7084a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertical Axis">
  <data key="d0">Vertical Axis</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The central reference line relative to which the inclination angle alpha of the bars is measured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vector Arrow">
  <data key="d0">Vector Arrow</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A bold red downward-pointing arrow used to visually represent the external force F.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Engineering Textbook Illustrations">
  <data key="d0">Engineering Textbook Illustrations</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">A visual style utilizing clean black lines for structural elements and red for active forces, typical in educational materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1db4055b5d566c7d454787a7ff1515b7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Governing Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)">
  <data key="d0">Governing Ordinary Differential Equation (ODE)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A second-order linear ODE with constant coefficients representing the axial displacement field of a single prismatic bar subjected to a constant distributed axial line load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Displacement Field u(x)">
  <data key="d0">Axial Displacement Field u(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The spatial displacement field of a single prismatic bar, whose general solution involves integration constants determined by boundary conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Represents the axial displacement at a position x along a hanging bar, calculated using a quadratic variation and a characteristic displacement scale.&lt;SEP&gt;The longitudinal displacement function along a structural member, obtained by solving the governing differential equation, with u(l) denoting displacement at the free end and u(0) at the fixed end.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-460d07ec9180c3a338bcc5988e8e42a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Single Prismatic Bar">
  <data key="d0">Single Prismatic Bar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural element, also known as Einzelstab, analyzed under a constant distributed axial line load such as self-weight.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constant Distributed Axial Line Load">
  <data key="d0">Constant Distributed Axial Line Load</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A load, or Streckenlast, applied along the length of the bar, encoded on the right-hand side of the equation as $-n = -G/l$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Total Weight Force">
  <data key="d0">Total Weight Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The self-weight or Eigengewicht of the bar, represented by $G$, which determines the distributed load and maximum tension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="One-dimensional Equilibrium Condition">
  <data key="d0">One-dimensional Equilibrium Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mechanical condition $N'(x) + n(x) = 0$ which, when combined with the constitutive law, gives rise to the governing ODE.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Linear-elastic Constitutive Law">
  <data key="d0">Linear-elastic Constitutive Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The relationship $N = EA \cdot \varepsilon = EA \cdot u'$ combined with the equilibrium condition to derive the governing ODE.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="General Solution u(x)">
  <data key="d0">General Solution u(x)</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The twice-integrated result of the governing ODE, given by $u(x) = -\frac{G}{2EA \cdot l}x^2 + C_1 x + C_2$, defining the axial displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stabtragwerk Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Stabtragwerk Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural bar analysis where the governing ODE provides the mathematical basis for computing stress distributions and elongation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784896993</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Longitudinal Coordinate x">
  <data key="d0">Longitudinal Coordinate x</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The spatial coordinate measured downward from the fixed end of the bar, along which the axial displacement varies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-1dfca5c7dbae86836330061b0f49bc01</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
