</node>
<node id="Material Models">
  <data key="d0">Material Models</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Models (also referred to as constitutive laws) describing the physical relationship between stress and strain, which are dependent on the material.&lt;SEP&gt;Theoretical representations of material behavior, studied alongside elastostatics using data from tensile or compression tests.&lt;SEP&gt;Abstract representations of material behavior (Stoffmodelle) whose determination is explicitly stated to be possible only through experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Definitions and models related to material behavior discussed in the academic material.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7191762e3c837260ad5bf3f1bc50f25a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb8c329536d2e721390485300fec34e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-783555881f4ab73d4d04ea548b9fae1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b35bef5073db0c5a31b6dd2e83c0ddb</data>
