</node>
<node id="Δl = α_T · ΔT · l">
  <data key="d0">Δl = α_T · ΔT · l</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Equation describing the thermal expansion of a rod or bar element, representing the change in length due to a uniform temperature change when no mechanical normal force is present (N = 0)</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Δl = ∫₀ˡ (N/(EA) + α_T ΔT) dx">
  <data key="d0">Δl = ∫₀ˡ (N/(EA) + α_T ΔT) dx</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">General elongation formula presented in the Zusammenfassung (summary) section, from which the specialized thermal expansion equation is derived</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ε_T = α_T · ΔT">
  <data key="d0">ε_T = α_T · ΔT</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal strain component whose integration over the length of the bar yields the thermal expansion equation Δl = α_T · ΔT · l</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermoelasticity">
  <data key="d0">Thermoelasticity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Field of study concerned with interactions between thermal and mechanical strain, for which the principle of superposition is fundamental&lt;SEP&gt;Framework combining mechanical and thermal effects for axially loaded members, encompassing constitutive relationships</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ab72d2dd30449c995d80393a0354227</data>
