  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elasticity Law">
  <data key="d0">Elasticity Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Known as Elastizitätsgesetz, one of the three conditions that must be considered simultaneously in statically indeterminate bar systems&lt;SEP&gt;The English translation of "Elastizitätsgesetz", a topic covered in Chapter 12 of the academic document&lt;SEP&gt;A primary subject area focused on in Chapter 12.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical principle governing material elasticity covered in the academic document.&lt;SEP&gt;The physical principle describing the relationship between stress and strain in a material.&lt;SEP&gt;Constitutive relationship discussed in Section 12.2 forming the complete linear elastic material model for homogeneous, isotropic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The kinematic basis in Section 12.2 where stresses and strains are related through material parameters, also known as Elastizitätsgesetz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd468369fbd1eac6b7662866f9ac8fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28d530475b93e04e7d6582c02926072c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d89ad2ee139d73e0b1367cc96d8b93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b37ac6d222ba4898f7b2f8f457e77e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbe1099c718b59c4f95b165b71f72ab</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998770</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constitutive Relationship">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Relationship</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A relationship combining mechanical and thermal effects in the framework of thermoelasticity for axially loaded members, of which the thermal expansion equation forms a part&lt;SEP&gt;An equation, G = E/[2(1+ν)], that connects shear strain to normal strains along the principal directions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-370a72fe18982a27d4543ffa0c4c20f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-529957e83da207a93efc376cc085ff93</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Axial Stress Distribution Equation">
  <data key="d0">Axial Stress Distribution Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical equation in LaTeX describing axial stress distribution σ(x) along a hanging rod under its own weight under statically determinate conditions, with formula σ(x) = N(x)/A = (G/A)(1 - x/l).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C₁">
  <data key="d0">C₁</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The integration constant derived from boundary conditions u(x=0) = 0 and u'(x=l) = 0, yielding C₁ = G.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastostatic Theory">
  <data key="d0">Elastostatic Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The theoretical framework within which the constitutive relationship between internal force, geometry, and stress is established for axially loaded bars.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="σ_max">
  <data key="d0">σ_max</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The maximum stress at the fixed end (x = 0) of the rod, equal to G/A, where the entire weight of the rod is supported and the critical cross-section for failure analysis is located.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Governing Differential Equation For Rod Displacement">
  <data key="d0">Governing Differential Equation For Rod Displacement</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The differential equation for rod displacement that, when integrated with specific boundary conditions, yields the axial stress distribution equation and the integration constant C₁.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ρ">
  <data key="d0">ρ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The density of the rod material, used in calculating the total weight G = ρgAl.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="g">
  <data key="d0">g</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The gravitational acceleration, used in calculating the total weight G = ρgAl.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
