</node>
<node id="Technische Spannung">
  <data key="d0">Technische Spannung</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">German term for 'Engineering stress,' calculated using the original (undeformed) cross-sectional area of the material.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wahre Spannung">
  <data key="d0">Wahre Spannung</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">German term for 'True stress,' calculated using the actual deformed cross-sectional area of the material during loading.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7a438fa813ee176d3e3d64cd5a7e2dba</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ortsabhängig Veränderliche Querschnittsfläche">
  <data key="d0">Ortsabhängig Veränderliche Querschnittsfläche</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">German term for 'location-dependent variable cross-sectional area,' discussed on page 7 in the context of analyzing rod elements under deformation.</data>
