<node id="Isotropic Materials">
  <data key="d0">Isotropic Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Materials for which the fourth-order elasticity tensor reduces to two independent parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials whose elastic constants demonstrate a profound interdependence, such as Young's Modulus, Shear Modulus, and Poisson's ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials in which temperature changes produce only normal strains and no shear strains.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials where temperature changes cause only normal strains and no shear strains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a093ad0a488172322e66eed43c540981&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f4c091fae29a6bd21771fd542eb9801</data>
