<node id="Kinematic Relations">
  <data key="d0">Kinematic Relations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equations describing geometric compatibility and deformation, forming one part of the three-equation system for structural analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Equations describing strain-displacement relationships, representing one of the three equation types for bar problems.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Kinematik, one of the three governing equation types required for structural analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific mechanical relations presented on the slide, which are traced to an authoritative source.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical equations, such as ε_ij = ½(∂u_i/∂x_j + ∂u_j/∂x_i), used to yield strain components from the partial derivatives of displacement components.</data>
