<node id="Superposition Method">
  <data key="d0">Superposition Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A structural analysis approach where mechanical displacement u_c^(1) cancels out the thermal displacement u_c^(0), paralleling the compatibility condition approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A method used for solving structural mechanics problems, specifically in the context of statically indeterminate systems.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique illustrated in the schematic used for solving statically indeterminate structural mechanics problems.&lt;SEP&gt;A method where the solution decomposes into a statically determinate thermal expansion (System 0) plus a correction from the redundant support reaction (System 1).&lt;SEP&gt;A method used to decompose the solution for statically indeterminate structural systems into multiple states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f99cae1296009661e572167acf5fe19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbd27ba75933ee3cba54b55605c1c8dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6428916bed03d77d29954942400a6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c71f393772a794391e49730d47a8bda4</data>
