<node id="Support Reactions">
  <data key="d0">Support Reactions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The unknown reactions B and C at the supports of the doubly clamped rod, determined by solving the compatibility equation for the internal axial force N.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactions at structural supports determined through superposition of statically determinate systems (System 0 and System 1).&lt;SEP&gt;The forces (such as the compressive reaction forces) generated at the supports of a structure, calculated for the statically indeterminate system under a thermal load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a907de5d496ddcf9ab58b307c8f8ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df979c16e8c52bf800fb84c3a4a4bdea</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Boundary Condition">
  <data key="d0">Boundary Condition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The geometric constraint Δl = Δl_1 + Δl_2 = 0 evaluated by the compatibility equation for a doubly clamped rod to prevent any net movement.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mechanical Displacement">
  <data key="d0">Mechanical Displacement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The displacement denoted as u_c^(1) that cancels out thermal displacement according to the superposition method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Displacement">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Displacement</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The displacement denoted as u_c^(0) that is canceled out by mechanical displacement according to the superposition method.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation ε = σ/E">
  <data key="d0">Equation ε = σ/E</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical equation representing the inverse formulation of Hooke's Law for uniaxial linear-elastic material behavior, establishing that strain is directly proportional to applied stress with Young's modulus serving as the inverse scaling factor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Proportional Limit Stress">
  <data key="d0">Proportional Limit Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The upper bound stress value σ_p within which the linear relationship between stress and strain remains valid.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-677c3b37a16b17c8907603bf39babaae</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="N">
  <data key="d0">N</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The internal normal force (Normalkraft) induced in a statically indeterminate two-segment bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Statically Indeterminate Two-Segment Bar">
  <data key="d0">Statically Indeterminate Two-Segment Bar</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A bar with two segments fixed at both ends, where segment 1 has cross-sectional area A1 and segment 2 has area A2.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Stiffness">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Stiffness</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stiffness of the series arrangement, calculated as EA1A2/(A1+A2), which is analogous to the harmonic mean of individual stiffnesses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Force Equation">
  <data key="d0">Normal Force Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The mathematical expression derived to determine the internal normal force N in the bar based on material and thermal properties.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Thermal Stress Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Stress Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An analytical method that uses the generalized Hooke's law formulation, particularly for constrained components.&lt;SEP&gt;An engineering application of the thermoelastic bar equation, specifically used for evaluating systems that are statically indeterminate.&lt;SEP&gt;A field of application for this analysis, including use in composite structures, bi-metallic systems, prestressed concrete design, and aerospace components.&lt;SEP&gt;Analytical examples discussed in the textbook involving stresses induced by thermal expansion effects in structural elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The process of evaluating stresses and forces within a material or structure caused by changes in temperature.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2866a3f417ff78b075338fa558392e29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb28b0e78717850205497e7c5e164dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64ae8f78050d6e3fb28375ca609b6390&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compressive Normal Force">
  <data key="d0">Compressive Normal Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The type of internal force induced by heating when thermal expansion is constrained by fixed supports.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Harmonic Mean">
  <data key="d0">Harmonic Mean</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical calculation to which the equivalent stiffness of the series arrangement is analogous.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical average to which the effective axial stiffness of the two-segment bar in series is analogous, scaled by Young's modulus.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-c38a79e5e8255bb32751c63ad9a1aca1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed4c24e6b357be46b6c720d32cdb5f62</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784897007</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
