  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A differential segment of a structural bar with length dx, represented as a light green-filled rectangle in the diagram, used to analyze equilibrium conditions in elastostatics.&lt;SEP&gt;A shaded gray right-angled triangle representing a wedge of thickness 't' cut from a thin plate, featuring vertical, horizontal, and inclined faces.&lt;SEP&gt;A small physical element on which stress transformation equations are analyzed in continuum mechanics&lt;SEP&gt;A differential rectangular element of width dx and height dy used in continuum mechanics to analyze stress and equilibrium at a point in a body.&lt;SEP&gt;A differential volume in solid mechanics within which static equilibrium is established.&lt;SEP&gt;A differential element extracted from a plate or disc, used to analyze plane stress conditions and mechanical equilibrium.</data>
