<node id="Koordinatentransformation">
  <data key="d0">Koordinatentransformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Koordinatentransformation is the German term for coordinate transformation, a fundamental concept extensively discussed within the field of mechanics and stress analysis. In the context of the provided source document, it is specifically addressed in Section 11.2.1 (spanning pages 16 to 18) of a German mechanics textbook. This section focuses on the mathematical and geometric foundations of transforming stress tensors between rotated coordinate systems.

As a systematic method, Koordinatentransformation utilizes tensor rotation to determine the normal and shear stresses acting on arbitrarily oriented cutting planes. The academic text details the derivation of these specific stress transformation equations for plane stress states, employing various trigonometric identities to calculate the transformed stress components accurately. This analytical process provides a geometric basis for understanding stress variations and can be visually represented by Mohr's stress circle. 

Furthermore, the discussion of Koordinatentransformation in this academic text includes the examination of the mathematical invariants of the stress tensor, specifically the expressions (σx + σy) and (σxσy - τxy²). It also explores the hydrostatic stress state as a distinct special case, ensuring a comprehensive understanding of how material stresses behave and are calculated under varying spatial orientations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdbbf7d68148fe88c3174f0ea8e4742&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdf4cd832b592c8035347d2e6e3804e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-011c3fc433230965d7a734e4052f7689&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3186598e4d31ef04b0826dc0b3dad17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788996859590fcaca4ffb066d7148714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2f298ccb33e1f76a031a29e81e1f9dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b5475536a7fccb42b9f6f9e39d32b77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87396546f57986339f19784a816ba8db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a03cb4a8bcb2904e74a15376b18fddec</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903956</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
