<node id="Kartesisches Koordinatensystem">
  <data key="d0">Kartesisches Koordinatensystem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A coordinate system whose coordinate planes are aligned with the mutually perpendicular sectional areas used to define the stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784900562</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hauptschubspannungen">
  <data key="d0">Hauptschubspannungen</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hauptschubspannungen is the German language term for principal shear stresses, representing the extreme or maximum values of shear stresses at a specific point within the field of continuum mechanics. These extremal shear stresses can be determined graphically using Mohr's stress circle. Mathematically, they are found by solving the stationary condition where the derivative dτ_ξη/dφ equals zero.

A defining characteristic of Hauptschubspannungen is that at the planes or sections where these extreme shear stresses occur, the normal stresses generally do not vanish. The methods for the calculation of these extremal shear stresses are commonly detailed in technical literature, including specific coverage in section 11.2.2 of relevant documents. Furthermore, within the principal stress framework, it is noted that equations related to these stresses may occasionally appear as garbled or transcription-erroneous forms in source materials, highlighting the need for careful analysis when evaluating their mathematical derivation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5db8101dd80f03fc824342c78093902c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8735ecf72f07b4cd7b82e22f492ade68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56ba60dee95d9f5127479d5f80c141c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6546507247b4802eb945e2a493cb040&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada0944efa350d49f7642c228e06590&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97b33a57b26cea4acd1fcb9fd8389687</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903997</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
