</node>
<node id="Shear Stress τ_xy">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress τ_xy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stress component representing the shear force per unit area acting on a surface, appearing in the equilibrium equations as a partial derivative term with respect to position.&lt;SEP&gt;The shear stress acting on the vertical face, resolved into the ξ-direction.&lt;SEP&gt;A shear stress component in the original coordinate system, used in the transformation equations, invariant I₂ definition, and the condition for principal directions tan(2φ*) = 2τ_xy/(σ_x - σ_y).&lt;SEP&gt;The shear stress in the x-y coordinate system that vanishes when evaluated on the principal axes.&lt;SEP&gt;A shear stress component whose differential variation across element dimensions is considered in the equilibrium equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress component related to shear strain through the shear modulus.&lt;SEP&gt;The shear stress component acting on the xy-plane, defined as force per unit area parallel to the surface in the constitutive relation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fa545fe4bb1d6483b658ddec935e5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372d45ee57b3e8dd4b75b8ce18594fad</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999179</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress σ_y">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress σ_y</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A stress component representing the normal force per unit area in the y-direction, appearing in the equilibrium equations with spatial derivatives.&lt;SEP&gt;The normal stress on the horizontal face of the triangular element.&lt;SEP&gt;A normal stress component in the original coordinate system, used in the transformation equations and invariant definitions.&lt;SEP&gt;A surface force arising from normal stresses acting on element boundaries in the y-direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7fa545fe4bb1d6483b658ddec935e5f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
