<node id="Principal Stresses">
  <data key="d0">Principal Stresses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Principal Stresses, also referred to by the German term *Hauptspannungen*, represent a fundamental and complex engineering mechanics concept within solid mechanics, structural engineering, and the strength of materials. They are defined as the extreme (maximum and minimum) normal stresses acting on a material element at a given point. These stresses occur on specific planes, known as principal planes, where the shear stress components are exactly zero. Mathematically, principal stresses are the eigenvalues of the Cauchy stress tensor and are conventionally denoted as σ₁, σ₂, and σ₃, with σ₁ being greater than σ₂ in two-dimensional analyses. Together, these three stress components define a general three-dimensional stress state.

The determination of these stresses relies heavily on stress transformation theory. Analytically, they are derived by extremizing the normal stress with respect to a rotation angle φ, utilizing the relation tan2φ* = 2τxy / (σx - σy). Mathematically, the principal stresses can be expressed using the first stress invariant as σ₁,₂ = I₁/2 ± √(I₁²/4 - I₂). Graphically, principal stresses are visualized and determined using Mohr's Stress Circle. The specific stress values σ₁ and σ₂ correspond to the points where Mohr's Circle intersects the horizontal σ-axis. In biaxial loading cases involving equal and opposite loads, the normal stresses in the y and x directions are indicated on the horizontal axis as +σ and -σ, respectively. Their values can be calculated directly from the circle's center (σM) and radius (R) using the formula σ₁,₂ = σM ± R. Furthermore, the orientations of these maximum and minimum normal stresses are dictated by the angular relationships present in Mohr's Circle. It is worth noting that in digitized educational materials, the symbols for these stresses defining a 3D continuum are occasionally subject to OCR misreads, mistakenly being identified as geometric angles such as ∠A₁, ∠A₂, or ∠B₁.

The nature of Principal Stresses varies depending on the specific loading and stress state of the material. In a uniaxial tensile test, the stress state is defined by σ₁ = σ_V while σ₂ = σ₃ = 0. Under a triaxial stress state, the arithmetic mean of the three principal stress components defines the hydrostatic stress. In a pure hydrostatic stress state, all principal stresses become equal (σ₁ = σ₂ = σ₃ = σ₀) and are equated to a single scalar value. This equality causes Mohr's Circle to degenerate into a single point on the horizontal axis, rendering every direction a principal direction. Conversely, in practical applications such as thin-walled pressure vessels under a plane stress state, the longitudinal (tangential) and circumferential (hoop) stresses act directly as the principal stresses because no shear stresses occur on those respective planes.

Identifying principal stresses is a critical analytical step preceding the establishment of equilibrium conditions, serving as an essential metric for evaluating structural failure and material yielding criteria. They are integral to the mathematical formulations associated with the derivation of the Distortion Energy Hypothesis (or distortion energy theory) and the calculation of equivalent stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e6a6756f3e11958caa7f25916a94bb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5f08150d01a4afad6a7e20e54169ec1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1678f499f1d6db4c88e28c21ca3f7ac4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5db8101dd80f03fc824342c78093902c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd62b02c985c73748d5224a5c1f6aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e0e1d2a168869746758dfc06077ca50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da8ea347d2fe041d08bb85c59209fc9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780797c1d45f39538f2b68c98e007f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c2c59e0f6a23f968e67f68fc9498278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80068bee1bee4c2ec1a3ff3d5d6d4f71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05f0cba91a41b2018384acbb7174e398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ac1dafe6c2621a4fb3a412b3493553&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2839b8d3cca96c984fc98ff0599ca3a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f2990ab5263ad174ce6fec37fef1115&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-379e0ab80e418646d3bbaa7c2a022894&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85630b6d3d048fd50a738bf6456c479f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8be23ae96862171a1f9cb78cb1cfcb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea236c2c090948676eebcd4986bd6df7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0bd290e24d36ba227108f0e9b5c1965e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edcede9e6d28ea1431d1d8fe530b301d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee3c8346d073a8fddaf35535eb1158c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012dfb2f1f77750672c0c98cb5c5f782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dbabf4bbc38075b362efc1cf68c92ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d77ac531ca72db1dfb705ad40ac98c3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5a136f98019f0bd369d2b6d44879f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-350755d5c7a3a740e91d107394468b5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f852bec3a8e229cf7fc9b647545ae29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecddc3be14bd893c4f22755acfb1f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-269e2be218f17e48feb7ecb2c0ddf3f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9c3492ddaae5a544709ab9626c48a75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14e4d70cf188ab298b97a6d1cf9e80c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd7867c7c2376ea56c7780cb73e5ec8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16cb12dda8d30577bdf35b6755d86117&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-154d19114c3f301c7c7a909d141ce692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a305b8793d9f114323bcd40953cba6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8557dd78e46c36e30dd3fe520b64408c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a30bb490f8e8f9e0d00884e4cba69c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2ada8da0499542e52dd4b0404a4d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68f46a2f336e00af32ab51674b243da4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af524c4a39d0752767ee95f685a1fb6b</data>
