  <data key="d0">2D Plane Stress Element Diagram (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram depicts a 2D differential stress element showing the components of the stress tensor—normal stresses ($\\sigma_x, \\sigma_y$) and shear stresses ($\\tau_{xy}, \\tau_{yx}$)—relative to a standard x-y coordinate system. It serves as the primary visual aid for Section 11.2.1 on coordinate transformation, illustrating the basis for defining a second-order tensor whose components transform predictably under rotation while maintaining physical invariants.</data>
