  <data key="d0">Stress Component Diagram for Coordinate Transformation (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram depicts an infinitesimal 2D stress element oriented within a rotated ξ-η coordinate system at an angle φ. It identifies the transformed normal stresses (σ_ξ, σ_η) and shear stresses (τ_ξη, τ_ηξ). The image directly supports the technical text regarding 'Koordinatentransformation' by providing the visual reference needed to understand how stress tensor components are projected onto inclined planes, illustrating the rotational invariance of the underlying physical stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-3cdbbf7d68148fe88c3174f0ea8e4742</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784901716</data>
</node>
