</node>
<node id="Coordinate Rotation">
  <data key="d0">Coordinate Rotation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The operation of rotating the coordinate system using trigonometric identities, central to stress tensor transformation.&lt;SEP&gt;The transformation under which the component values of the stress tensor change while the physical state remains invariant.&lt;SEP&gt;The transformation of the coordinate system under which the stress tensor invariants I₁ and I₂ remain constant.&lt;SEP&gt;A transformation under which the strain tensor exhibits proper transformation behavior, ensured by the critical factor of 1/2 converting engineering shear strains to tensorial components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbe1099c718b59c4f95b165b71f72ab</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999191</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Variable 'v'">
  <data key="d0">Variable 'v'</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The variable in the incomplete equation that could represent a tensor invariant, Poisson's ratio, or a transformation parameter depending on the context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2D Stress Analysis">
  <data key="d0">2D Stress Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A branch of stress analysis where the first invariant I₁ and second invariant I₂ are defined.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Querkontraktionszahl">
  <data key="d0">Querkontraktionszahl</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The German engineering term for Poisson's ratio, representing the transverse strain ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio, a dimensionless quantity characterizing the transverse contraction of a material.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio ν, a material parameter used in Hooke's model&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio, a material constant discussed within the plane stress state section of the elasticity law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cd1f71b01c1aa5c67c36a16a597748fb&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00185afb9a5d259c31643f50551104c4</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
