  <data key="d2">An advanced engineering mechanics concept discussed in the technical content surrounding the citation.&lt;SEP&gt;A continuum mechanics concept, also known as Spannungstensor, involving tensor symmetry and moment equilibriums as mathematical formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;A technical mechanics concept discussed in the document, relating to the analysis of stress in materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Spannungstensor, an engineering mechanics concept involving tensor analysis of stress, discussed in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical object describing stress, whose content aligns with the strain state material in the textbook.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical concept used in theoretical stress analysis that connects to the Festigkeitshypothesen framework</data>
