</node>
<node id="Mohr's Circle">
  <data key="d0">Mohr's Circle</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mohr's Circle, also known by its German names Mohrscher Spannungskreis, Spannungskreis, or Verzerrungskreis, is a foundational graphical, geometric, and analytical method used in continuum mechanics, solid mechanics, engineering mechanics, and materials science. It serves as a comprehensive theoretical tool and technical diagram used to represent, analyze, and perform coordinate transformations of the state of stress and strain at a specific point within a material. By mapping the state of stress as a locus of points in a Cartesian coordinate system, it provides a visual alternative that simplifies complex algebraic stress transformation equations.

In its standard construction, which is derived from the symmetric 2D Cauchy stress tensor and kinematic compatibility equations, normal stress is plotted on the horizontal axis, and shear stress is plotted on the vertical axis. The center of the circle is located at the mean stress point. A defining geometric characteristic of Mohr's Circle is that angular relationships on the circle are doubled relative to physical space, a feature that directly dictates the orientation of principal stresses and yields the double-angle tensor transformation formulation.

Mohr's Circle is primarily utilized to determine critical stress values and their corresponding physical orientations. Principal stresses are found at the intersection points of the circle and the horizontal normal stress axis. The maximum shear stress is mathematically equal to the circle's radius and characteristically occurs on planes oriented at 45 degrees to the principal stress directions. This 45-degree relationship demonstrates that a biaxial stress state corresponds to pure shear at a 45-degree rotation of the coordinate system, where the shear stress equals the principal stress. Similarly, the method illustrates that in a uniaxial stress state, the maximum shear stress occurs on a plane at 45 degrees to the principal axis. The framework systematically evaluates these and other two-dimensional plane stress states, including the hydrostatic stress state, which causes the circle's radius to become zero and degenerate into a single point.

Beyond theoretical stress and strain analysis, Mohr's Circle is an indispensable technical tool in practical structural mechanics. It is employed to evaluate stress states in complex engineering scenarios, such as pressure vessel analysis, and to determine normal and shear stresses on arbitrary inclined sections. Furthermore, it is used to predict the yielding and failure of materials subjected to complex, multi-axial loading conditions. As a theoretical stress analysis tool, it precedes and connects directly to the Festigkeitshypothesen (failure hypotheses) framework, serving a critical role in the design and analysis of structures and mechanical components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-842c0517bb20a54922d1a75c277c68f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6513413e0a80f005888472d94d385e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-792f1aab7b01df3f4ae8fa499208a41a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-341774a38a3b4fd47c6656391af81dd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b44241248f288278ba7f5d8fa8160e3e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85ca1064506b38c8fe493e3ffc533c71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b2a42c115ed62e72e715daa89e2370&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7f241f746726b97e3dc567365e483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3780797c1d45f39538f2b68c98e007f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c2c59e0f6a23f968e67f68fc9498278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef86ae323cfba68764c2acb2d46785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97ae2381cfa6e993a16166b7495765c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74378ee7045b50cecf2c625c47685477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6ea2012f708d083bcf1f8357bfab292&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40562a8ce19d10e78736b201626c9b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05f0cba91a41b2018384acbb7174e398&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9d228101e892c4b9b284f5228fa25ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2662124ebaa998fdaa13ffecb3add380&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-153ac624cdef095260ab75841c027b8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3553477d678ccfb56c56a99c6a713a1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cae0fdb4f5af9a553af5e5ec7a633b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f56ba60dee95d9f5127479d5f80c141c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95309ae773a0c5fe9703868d35942eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b47aa4fc45ad067947c357da574f854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4df6ac3e36adc464a8f9e47b557ec07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f29928f565c2e69c