<node id="Circumferential Stress">
  <data key="d0">Circumferential Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The hoop stress σ_φ in the vessel wall, equal to twice the longitudinal stress (σ_φ = 2σ_x), representing the larger principal stress that causes longitudinal cracking failure.&lt;SEP&gt;The circumferential or hoop stress denoted as σφ, acting tangent to the circumference of the cylinder, identified as a principal stress in the biaxial stress state with no shear stress present.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as hoop stress ($\sigma_{\varphi}$), it is the stress in the vessel wall that resists internal pressure.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress $\sigma_\varphi$ in the circumferential (hoop) direction of the pressure vessel, resisting the vessel splitting lengthwise.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of stress calculated for the pressure vessel, denoted by the symbol σ_φ.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35913765c2d7101f6d284ecd039952ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee3c8346d073a8fddaf35535eb1158c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bd1d5444d931cb0efa80cdff770977&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aecddc3be14bd893c4f22755acfb1f21</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tangential Stress">
  <data key="d0">Tangential Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress ($\sigma_t$) in the spherical vessel wall, which equals the circumferential stress due to spherical symmetry.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of stress calculated for the pressure vessel, denoted by the symbol σ_t.&lt;SEP&gt;The tangential stress σ_t in the spherical vessel wall, equal to the hoop stress σ_φ due to spherical symmetry.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-35913765c2d7101f6d284ecd039952ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bd1d5444d931cb0efa80cdff770977</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903947</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
