<node id="Biaxial Stress State">
  <data key="d0">Biaxial Stress State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Biaxial Stress State is a two-dimensional state of stress occurring within an elastic material, characterized by stresses acting in two perpendicular directions. This condition is often analyzed at the level of a square material element, where stress is distributed across two orthogonal planes. Depending on the specific loading conditions, this state can involve a compressive principal stress acting in one direction while a tensile stress acts perpendicularly. Additionally, a biaxial stress state can consist of equal magnitudes of tension and compression acting on planes that are rotated by 45 degrees. As a fundamental two-dimensional condition, it allows for the mathematical derivation of relationships between fundamental elastic properties.

In engineering applications, the Biaxial Stress State is crucial because it governs the design and analysis of thin-walled pressure vessels. Within a thin-walled spherical pressure vessel under internal pressure, this state manifests as a uniform distribution of load in two perpendicular directions. Consequently, the tangential stress is equal to the circumferential stress. This balanced distribution is mathematically reflected by a factor of 1/2 in the spherical vessel formula. 

This uniform distribution contrasts with cylindrical vessels, which also experience a two-directional stress state but with unequal principal stresses; in the cylindrical case, the hoop stress carries twice the load of the longitudinal stress. Overall, the Biaxial Stress State provides a critical framework for visualizing and calculating the structural integrity of both fundamental material elements and complex pressurized containers.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-fb31546e781f11ba51b9575be2e9cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73adfabedf760785acfd7b799786f369&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1f8906173d951132fd77877e8868d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bd1d5444d931cb0efa80cdff770977&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd4685e0a0874c320cb468d922d54e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5deab09d1c9d30fa6463bb3156b4278</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999407</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
