<node id="Failure Criteria">
  <data key="d0">Failure Criteria</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Failure Criteria are a set of conditions or mathematical limits used to predict the failure or yielding of a material when subjected to complex loading conditions. As an advanced mechanics of materials concept, often referred to as Festigkeitshypothesen, these principles govern material failure by mathematically calibrating equivalent stress. They function as general theoretical rules essential for assessing structural integrity and material strength, acting as a central topic that cross-references and connects various analytical sections within continuum mechanics.

The application of Failure Criteria includes well-known theoretical rules such as the von Mises and Tresca criteria. These specific standards are widely utilized in structural analysis and material strength assessment. By evaluating computed stress states derived from analyses like biaxial stress, these criteria can effectively assess specific modes of material breakdown, including "Versagen durch Rissbildung" (failure through crack formation).

The theoretical foundation of Failure Criteria relies heavily on comprehensive stress analysis, which forms the crucial basis for these predictive rules. Understanding angular distortion resulting from shear strain is a key component of this analysis. Furthermore, the evaluation of these material failure standards utilizes fundamental concepts such as the first stress invariant. Because materials must be analyzed in different orientations, stress transformation equations serve as a fundamental step in this process. Ultimately, the study of plane stress states provides the necessary foundational framework upon which these subsequent analysis principles in material strength are built.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eb966affea49c8515afe80d893d4ba39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30fd62b02c985c73748d5224a5c1f6aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28e8a589d6ecd831cc0e1afc0b83e4bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1685984065ed0dcd54dea046d7d4f918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f852bec3a8e229cf7fc9b647545ae29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963728870ca7c1f5d880eae3e1e47f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db9317a3d674bad613adaf9f20eaf18d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57d772e71ccd830b12050844ec9eef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
