  <data key="d0">Maximum Shear Stresses</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The highest shear stresses experienced by a material at a given point, determined using stress transformation and Mohr's circle.&lt;SEP&gt;The highest shear stress values and their corresponding orientations determined graphically using Mohr's circle.&lt;SEP&gt;Maximum values of shear stress determined through stress transformation, critical for predicting material failure&lt;SEP&gt;Specific stress values determined using coordinate transformations, representing the largest shear stress at a point.&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum shear stress values at a point, determined through Mohr's circle construction as part of practical engineering stress analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34f056013d274101fd8fe012cf408b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b625d3948531b3dcd9b53a158a3a5265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf5a136f98019f0bd369d2b6d44879f8</data>
