</node>
<node id="Double Angle">
  <data key="d0">Double Angle</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An angle, specifically twice the rotation angle, used within the trigonometric functions that weight the stress variables in the transformation equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784903990</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second-order Tensor">
  <data key="d0">Second-order Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical object representing stress, rigorously established through stress transformation analysis as independent of coordinate system&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical classification of the stress state, expressing its physical principle in solid mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-68094852a469c1054fde9d0f452e6077&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e</data>
