<node id="Pure Shear">
  <data key="d0">Pure Shear</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A special case analyzed within the context of Mohr's Stress Circle.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress state related to uniaxial tension when considering planes inclined at 45 degrees.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress state equivalent to a state of equal tension and compression in orthogonal directions, occurring on planes inclined at 45 degrees.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific state of stress that corresponds to a biaxial stress state where σ₁ = σ and σ₂ = -σ when examined at a 45° rotation of the coordinate system.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress state that transforms into equal biaxial principal stresses (σ_x = -σ_y) when analyzed in a 45°-rotated coordinate system.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific loading condition that, along with equivalent biaxial loading, causes the angular distortion of an element.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific state of stress that occurs when normal stresses are transformed under a specific geometric rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6e0e1d2a168869746758dfc06077ca50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f7f241f746726b97e3dc567365e483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-818241f00ae24dac642bd60f22620196&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2fbc89309c5fa28f062356d8fd0dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c4b387a69caef33cbbc0d01cd946a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963728870ca7c1f5d880eae3e1e47f0f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
