<node id="Projected Area">
  <data key="d0">Projected Area</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The area onto which forces are projected using trigonometric functions to calculate their components&lt;SEP&gt;The projected area denoted as 2r · Δl, representing the vertical area on which the internal pressure p acts in the longitudinal section view of panel d.&lt;SEP&gt;The specific surface area of the vessel used to calculate the total pressure force in the vertical direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e80e31b80a7c1439506d701b5bbac342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82d26e50b1a6b9a189224f9805e4217e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Resisting Force">
  <data key="d0">Resisting Force</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The force exerted by the vessel wall against internal pressure, represented on the left-hand side of the longitudinal stress equation.&lt;SEP&gt;The force generated by the wall stresses that counteracts the pressure force to maintain equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e80e31b80a7c1439506d701b5bbac342&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee3c8346d073a8fddaf35535eb1158c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tensor Symmetry">
  <data key="d0">Tensor Symmetry</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical formulation related to stress tensors in continuum mechanics, presented in the main text.&lt;SEP&gt;A property of the strain tensor where components satisfy the condition ε_ij = ε_ji, ensuring symmetric matrix representation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5a5bec24cc4d96b66479607814f58f26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddbe1099c718b59c4f95b165b71f72ab</data>
