</node>
<node id="2D Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d0">2D Stress Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress tensor whose eigenvalues are the principal stresses, with invariants I₁ (trace) and I₂ (determinant) remaining constant under coordinate rotation.&lt;SEP&gt;A two-dimensional stress tensor whose eigenvalues yield the principal stresses σ₁ and σ₂</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fca9235e4f945947ddf250020a6f05e</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Invariant I₁">
  <data key="d0">Invariant I₁</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The first invariant of the 2D stress tensor equal to σ_x + σ_y (trace), remaining constant under coordinate rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Invariant I₂">
  <data key="d0">Invariant I₂</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The second invariant of the 2D stress tensor equal to σ_x·σ_y - τ_xy² (determinant), remaining constant under coordinate rotation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Characteristic Equation">
  <data key="d0">Characteristic Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The equation σ² - I₁σ + I₂ = 0 that yields the principal stress values σ₁,₂ = I₁/2 ± √(I₁²/4 - I₂).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Section Angle φ">
  <data key="d0">Section Angle φ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The angle parameter used in the transformation equations for plane stress, defining the orientation of the stress section.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress σ_ξ">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress σ_ξ</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A normal stress component defined as (σ_x + σ_y)/2 + (σ_x - σ_y)/2 · cos(2φ) + τ_xy · sin(2φ).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress σ_η">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress σ_η</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A normal stress component defined as (σ_x + σ_y)/2 - (σ_x - σ_y)/2 · cos(2φ) - τ_xy · sin(2φ).&lt;SEP&gt;The transformed normal stress evaluated at the principal angle, which yields one of the principal stresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Stress τ_ξη">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress τ_ξη</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A shear stress component defined as -(σ_x - σ_y)/2 · sin(2φ) + τ_xy · cos(2φ).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904030</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress σ_x">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress σ_x</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal stress acting on the vertical face of the triangular element, contributing to the equilibrium equation.&lt;SEP&gt;A normal stress component in the original coordinate system, used in the transformation equations and invariant definitions.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal stress component in x-direction acting on the faces of an infinitesimal element, with spatial gradient ∂σ_x/∂x describing its variation</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0658f7561c12b0a53196517bdee01443&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8</data>
