<node id="Scheibe">
  <data key="d0">Scheibe</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">"Scheibe" is a German term for a disk or plate, widely utilized in solid mechanics to describe a two-dimensional planar structural element or surface-like body. Characterized by having a small thickness relative to its overall side lengths, it is often modeled as a thin, rectangular solid body or a biaxially loaded plate. The "Scheibe" serves as the primary geometric model for defining the plane stress state under in-plane loading conditions, making it fundamental for illustrating the deformation of area-shaped bodies.

When subjected to biaxial loads, the "Scheibe" undergoes two-dimensional deformation and axial changes, with its overall stress state commonly analyzed to derive the relationship between elastic constants. In elasticity considerations, the shape change of this surface body—which involves a position-dependent displacement vector of neighboring material points—is frequently predicted using linear approximations and finite element analysis.

To facilitate stress analysis and the derivation of constitutive laws under simultaneous multi-directional strains, infinitesimal elements are extracted from the "Scheibe." Specifically, infinitesimal rectangular or triangular material elements are cut out from the disk to analyze stress equilibrium. Therefore, while the "Scheibe" primarily functions as a macroscopic planar body experiencing two-dimensional deformation, the term is also applied to the two-dimensional differential material element itself that is isolated for rigorous mechanical evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7e48d7926a99342f43a9d78825059455&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef86ae323cfba68764c2acb2d46785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae7aec8cf21235bd79c851b9cc6978f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49e2cb25fd70f2b5f3b6c22629fe461a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1685984065ed0dcd54dea046d7d4f918&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20d2489764cb6b004e3ff06ba7ebe0c1&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f01ffec0f2bc0b862fdc1a6a3126dbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646c9364260cc8f0c76b71d04358c907&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdf7262993e514ad26ba97ab4f2a420&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc328ffaca84d39a7bfc9df7c2f37086&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998973</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
  <data key="d7">Scheibe</data>
</node>
