<node id="Point M">
  <data key="d0">Point M</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The center point of the infinitesimal quader where the state of stress is being analyzed, marked with a small circle in the diagram&lt;SEP&gt;The center point of the material element, where the origin of the local coordinate system coincides.&lt;SEP&gt;The geometric center of an infinitesimal volume element, used as the specific reference point for evaluating the moment equilibrium.&lt;SEP&gt;The center of Mohr's Circle located on the sigma-axis, representing the average normal stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The center point of Mohr's Circle located on the horizontal σ-axis, from which radii and angles are measured.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-d90be9fb874d21dec7e04ccacce0f39e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb64a0edb671186691ad9f74cd07ae9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb9e40b1a13627933f97ce043e59f768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b23912fb95dffaea41a466afd896e511</data>
