<node id="Minor Principal Stress σ₂">
  <data key="d0">Minor Principal Stress σ₂</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The minimum normal stress acting on a material element when oriented along the principal axes, where shear stress vanishes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress Components σ_x And σ_y">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress Components σ_x And σ_y</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The original Cartesian normal stress components in the x-y coordinate system.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrostatic Term">
  <data key="d0">Hydrostatic Term</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The isotropic term ½(σ_x + σ_y) in the stress transformation equation representing the average normal stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress-Tensor Invariant">
  <data key="d0">Stress-Tensor Invariant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A property of the stress tensor that remains unchanged under rotation, specifically referring to the hydrostatic term.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deviatoric Correction Terms">
  <data key="d0">Deviatoric Correction Terms</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Terms involving cos(2φ*) and sin(2φ*) that redistribute stress magnitude based on orientation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Eigenvalue Analysis">
  <data key="d0">Eigenvalue Analysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical procedure used for principal stress determination.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical procedure used to determine principal stresses from a stress tensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95309ae773a0c5fe9703868d35942eff</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="2D Cauchy Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d0">2D Cauchy Stress Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The mathematical object describing the state of stress in a two-dimensional plane, analyzed using eigenvalues.&lt;SEP&gt;A tensor describing the state of stress at a point in two dimensions, whose tensor invariants relate to the principal stresses and eigenvalue problem.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6643a9ec6dd9b81db5b4233bf1899ef</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Critical Loading Directions">
  <data key="d0">Critical Loading Directions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The specific orientations determined in engineering mechanics that result in extremal stress values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="X-Y Coordinate System">
  <data key="d0">X-Y Coordinate System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The original Cartesian reference frame used to define the initial stress components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
