<node id="Angular Momentum Balance">
  <data key="d0">Angular Momentum Balance</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A principle (Drall- oder Momentengleichgewicht) applied to an infinitesimal volume element, requiring that the resultant moment about any axis through the center of the element vanishes, leading to the symmetric stress tensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-012508b359d5f14b7a687dd269f97c12</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cauchy Stress Theory">
  <data key="d0">Cauchy Stress Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theory in continuum mechanics where the symmetry of the stress tensor is fundamental.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-012508b359d5f14b7a687dd269f97c12</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904048</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constitutive Equations">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Equations</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical equations formulated in solid mechanics, fluid dynamics, and finite element analysis, for which the symmetric stress tensor is essential.&lt;SEP&gt;Equations that relate stress and strain in linear elasticity theory. Their introduction is marked by page number 10 in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Equations describing the stress-strain relationships for linear elasticity, systematically derived in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Mathematical equations involved in the extended analytical derivation for linear elastic isotropic materials within Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-012508b359d5f14b7a687dd269f97c12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a3421094c08152da74a60f04257a266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47751b806b05c6d8ba7d4ccfae665886</data>
