  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A standard notation used for stress components where the first index identifies the plane's orientation via its normal vector, and the second index identifies the direction in which the stress component acts.&lt;SEP&gt;A notational convention used in engineering mechanics to represent stress tensors and stress components.&lt;SEP&gt;A notation convention used for representing stress components in stress tensor analysis.</data>
