<node id="Shear Stress Extremization Equation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress Extremization Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation representing the extremization of the shear stress transformation relation, found by taking the derivative of the shear stress formula with respect to the rotation angle and setting it to zero to find maximum and minimum values.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6589bf554e5066ac0fa2960ba8d673c0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Stress Transformation Relation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress Transformation Relation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A formula calculating the shear stress in a rotated coordinate system, defined as $\tau_{\xi\eta}(\varphi) = -½(\sigma_x - \sigma_y)\sin 2\varphi + \tau_{xy} \cos 2\varphi$.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6589bf554e5066ac0fa2960ba8d673c0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Principal Shear Stress">
