<node id="Rotated Coordinate System">
  <data key="d0">Rotated Coordinate System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A coordinate system rotated relative to the Cartesian system, labeled as ξ, η.&lt;SEP&gt;A secondary Cartesian coordinate system defined by the 'eta' axis (normal to the inclined hypotenuse) and the 'xi' axis (tangential to the hypotenuse).&lt;SEP&gt;A coordinate system, denoted as (ξ, η), that is rotated by a specific angle φ relative to the original (x, y) axes.&lt;SEP&gt;An alternative reference frame used to view a biaxial stress state, exploiting the equivalence of strain states according to Mohr's circle principle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-6589bf554e5066ac0fa2960ba8d673c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c2cf3a337f73c88af5880c2708e9c48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65f35adb2f34cbe81a9755002339ad40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999391</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
