</node>
<node id="Maximum Shear Stress (τ_max)">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Shear Stress (τ_max)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The maximum shear stress magnitude expressed as τ_max = |σ₁ - σ₂| / 2, relating to principal stresses in the principal axis system&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum shear stress in a thin-walled cylindrical pressure vessel under internal pressure, calculated as (1/4)·p·r/t, occurring on planes oriented at 45° to the principal stress directions&lt;SEP&gt;The maximum shear stress acting on any plane within a material element, acting as the amplitude of shear stress variation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dd747436c8f7ae4c9f1ad317397dda30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14e4d70cf188ab298b97a6d1cf9e80c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af588c739fd8cf2b760927ad23d5c9f8</data>
