<node id="Shear Stress (τ)">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress (τ)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of stress represented by the vertical axis in the Cartesian coordinate system of Mohr's Circle.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress component acting parallel to the surface of the material, found to equal the principal stress on 45° planes according to Mohr's circle.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear stress component, measured in units of pressure (Pa or N/m²).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-004e08ca4afebf77525a1d7810f76686</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999378</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Element">
  <data key="d0">Stress Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical element whose state of stress and rotation are analyzed using the angles depicted in Mohr's Circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5ca440e5727deb504109d3cda9b3642d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Numerator">
  <data key="d0">Numerator</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The top part of the equation: (1/2)(1 + 1/2)(10) = (1/2)(3/2)(10) = 7.5</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6546507247b4802eb945e2a493cb040</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Denominator">
  <data key="d0">Denominator</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The bottom part of the equation: (1/2 + 1/2)(1/2)(10) = (1)(1/2)(10) = 5</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6546507247b4802eb945e2a493cb040</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Result">
  <data key="d0">Result</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The final value of the equation: 7.5 ÷ 5 = 1.5 = 3/2</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b6546507247b4802eb945e2a493cb040</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
