  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Stress Component">
  <data key="d0">Shear Stress Component</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The stress component τ_xy acting tangential to surfaces, used in computing the radius of Mohr's Circle.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784904052</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Material Yielding">
  <data key="d0">Material Yielding</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A failure criterion dictated by the extremal stress values acting on an element.&lt;SEP&gt;The onset of plastic deformation in a material, predicted using the fundamental calculations established by Festigkeitshypothesen</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4734b30eabf1c888d7ceb2c9dd8d2f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999510</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Failure">
  <data key="d0">Structural Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">A failure mode dictated by the extremal stress values acting on an element.&lt;SEP&gt;The breakdown or yielding of a structure, predicted in structural and mechanical engineering by comparing calculated equivalent stress against the material's yield strength&lt;SEP&gt;The loss of load-bearing capacity or structural integrity, predicted using calculations derived from Festigkeitshypothesen</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bcd5ad0575ad16303ca4601a26ea32f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2ada8da0499542e52dd4b0404a4d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4734b30eabf1c888d7ceb2c9dd8d2f</data>
