<node id="Yield Strength">
  <data key="d0">Yield Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The material property that the principal stresses must not exceed to prevent catastrophic failure and rupture.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of material failure stress from uniaxial testing used to calculate admissible stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress threshold at which a material begins to deform plastically.&lt;SEP&gt;A material property determined from a uniaxial tensile test, against which the computed equivalent stress is compared to predict structural failure&lt;SEP&gt;A uniaxial material property against which multiaxial stress states are evaluated using Festigkeitshypothesen</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-aecddc3be14bd893c4f22755acfb1f21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-343794ade2b1d656c68e2c17454713f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b2ada8da0499542e52dd4b0404a4d97&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4734b30eabf1c888d7ceb2c9dd8d2f</data>
