<node id="Material Element">
  <data key="d0">Material Element</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A Material Element is a physical representation of an infinitesimal two-dimensional differential volume or a specific point within a material where internal forces are evaluated. It is fundamentally utilized in mechanics to analyze mechanical stresses—such as normal stresses acting on all four faces—exerted on a material that is under load. 

Visually, the Material Element is standardly depicted as a light-gray filled square or rectangle with a thin or solid black outline. It is commonly modeled within a Cartesian coordinate system to provide clear geometric and spatial context. In certain engineering contexts, particularly within German terminology, this differential section is also referred to as a 'Scheibe' (disk or plate).

To fully evaluate complex stress states and transformations, the Material Element is frequently illustrated at varying orientations rather than remaining stationary. It is commonly rotated counter-clockwise relative to a standard horizontal base by a specific angle. A frequent application of this visualization involves rotating the material element by exactly 45 degrees, which allows for the comprehensive analysis of how mechanical stresses act along different intersecting planes within the loaded material.&lt;SEP&gt;An element of material that undergoes deformation under specific loading conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-98f7f241f746726b97e3dc567365e483&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95ef86ae323cfba68764c2acb2d46785&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40562a8ce19d10e78736b201626c9b32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98ff466f481e3ef48f03b583574686cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe13321a6d5df3c82e760adc093a99c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb64a0edb671186691ad9f74cd07ae9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8be23ae96862171a1f9cb78cb1cfcb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012dfb2f1f77750672c0c98cb5c5f782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5302c423fc1b3994ee440aa1eba886af</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999354</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
