<node id="Verzerrungstensor">
  <data key="d0">Verzerrungstensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Strain tensor for the plane strain state (EVZ), with the main diagonal containing strains and the secondary diagonal containing half the shear strains.&lt;SEP&gt;The strain tensor that describes the deformation state at a point in a body, with 3x3 components in 3D, reducing to a 2x2 matrix in the plane strain state (EVZ)&lt;SEP&gt;The strain tensor describing the deformation state at a point of a body, having 3x3 components in spatial cases considering symmetry&lt;SEP&gt;A German term for the 2D strain tensor used to represent strain in material elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain tensors, a theoretical topic covered in Section 11.4 of the textbook describing the state of strain in a deformable body.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5b74b4caf274c8a818b5e7d868904b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-427b2f7911554c401a806ff733b5975e</data>
