<node id="Schubmodul">
  <data key="d0">Schubmodul</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The shear modulus of a material, which can be determined through a torsion test on a thin-walled tube&lt;SEP&gt;The shear modulus G, related to the elastic modulus E and Poisson's ratio ν by the equation G = E / (2(1+ν))&lt;SEP&gt;The shear modulus, a material constant for isotropic elastic materials, whose relationship to the modulus of elasticity is derived on page 13.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear modulus G, a material property whose relationship with Young's modulus is derived mathematically in Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear modulus, a material property discussed in Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz, whose relationship to Young's modulus (E-Modul) is derived using a biaxially loaded plate.&lt;SEP&gt;The German term for shear modulus, whose relationship with Young's modulus was introduced on page 16.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ab6bb09c88f34c57e39b028978709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47751b806b05c6d8ba7d4ccfae665886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec12900410ee6e1062ea25bf1aa27c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
