<node id="E-Modul">
  <data key="d0">E-Modul</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Young's modulus or modulus of elasticity, one of two independent material constants for isotropic elastic materials, related to the shear modulus&lt;SEP&gt;The modulus of elasticity, a material constant for isotropic elastic materials whose relationship to the shear modulus is derived on page 13 using a biaxially loaded plate.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus, also referred to as longitudinal elasticity, a material property whose relationship with shear modulus is derived mathematically in Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus, a material property discussed in Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz, whose relationship to the shear modulus is derived using a biaxially loaded plate.&lt;SEP&gt;The German term for Young's modulus, whose relationship with shear modulus was introduced on page 16.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ab6bb09c88f34c57e39b028978709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47751b806b05c6d8ba7d4ccfae665886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec12900410ee6e1062ea25bf1aa27c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bd5ab7377144955c4c6d31264ee5359</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normalspannungshypothese">
  <data key="d0">Normalspannungshypothese</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A strength hypothesis where the maximum normal stress is decisive for material stress, showing good agreement for brittle materials&lt;SEP&gt;Normal stress hypothesis stating that maximum normal stress governs material failure, showing good agreement with brittle materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Normal stress hypothesis or Rankine criterion, a strength hypothesis introduced on page 19, which is particularly applicable to brittle materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The normal stress hypothesis, a type of failure hypothesis mentioned in the surrounding text.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1a498a78500a61b206c4b1205b49030&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57d772e71ccd830b12050844ec9eef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b562c6cf8ea640066c4829c2dbc8a288</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
