  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784964350</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gestaltänderungsenergie">
  <data key="d0">Gestaltänderungsenergie</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The distortion energy equal to the total internal energy minus the hydrostatic energy portion, relevant for plastic deformation&lt;SEP&gt;The distortion energy isolated from the decomposition of total strain energy, theoretically equated to uniaxial equivalent stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as the hypothesis of shape change energy, it is a complex engineering mechanics concept discussed in the educational material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d4e48f780c214c48a682a8ccd2b8aa87-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a757fe6cf2d7246e4d34ad6c4db2db27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af524c4a39d0752767ee95f685a1fb6b</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Zulässige Spannung">
  <data key="d0">Zulässige Spannung</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The allowable stress introduced to prevent failure, requiring that stresses in a bar do not exceed this value</data>
