<node id="Diagram of Uniaxial Plate Deformation and Strain State (image)">
  <data key="d0">Diagram of Uniaxial Plate Deformation and Strain State (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram visualizes the 'Verzerrungszustand' (state of strain) in a plate subjected to uniaxial tension. It demonstrates how the orientation of a material element affects its deformation: square ①, aligned with the load, exhibits only normal strain (extension into a rectangle), while square ②, at a 45-degree angle, undergoes both normal and shear strain (distortion into a rhombus). The image includes the displacement vector 'u' from point P to P' and the applied tensile stress 'σ', serving to explain that displacement vectors are location-dependent and that shear components appear in non-principal orientations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-cf382350c1415b7ddd1f82959df3fdb7</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784971958</data>
</node>
