<node id="Two-Dimensional Displacement Vector Field (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Two-Dimensional Displacement Vector Field (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Defines the position-dependent displacement vector field r(x,y) for a 2D deformable body, decomposed into Cartesian components u(x,y) and v(x,y). Serves as the kinematic foundation for strain analysis, enabling derivation of strain tensors and forming the basis for Taylor series approximation of neighboring point displacements under small deformation assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784972205</data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement Vector Field Equation">
  <data key="d0">Displacement Vector Field Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation (in LaTeX format) that defines the displacement vector field for a two-dimensional deformable body, expressed as r(x,y) = u(x,y)·e_x + v(x,y)·e_y, serving as the starting point for deriving the infinitesimal strain tensor through partial differentiation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)">
  <data key="d0">Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A vector-valued function representing the displacement field of a planar body, expressed as a linear combination of Cartesian basis vectors e_x and e_y with scalar component functions u(x,y) and v(x,y) representing horizontal and vertical displacement components respectively.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998906</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Two-Dimensional Deformable Body (Scheibe)">
  <data key="d0">Two-Dimensional Deformable Body (Scheibe)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A planar body undergoing position-dependent deformation, analyzed within the context of strain analysis (Verzerrungszustand) in continuum mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998906</data>
