<node id="Strain-Displacement Relations">
  <data key="d0">Strain-Displacement Relations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Mathematical relations derived using Taylor series expansions under the assumption of small deformations, connecting displacement fields to strain measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Relations derived using a Taylor series expansion that describe small deformations by examining changes in side lengths and angles.&lt;SEP&gt;Kinematic equations that relate macroscopic deformations to the underlying displacement field, formulated using the simplified result α = ∂u/∂y.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Kinematikgleichungen, these kinematic equations serve as the geometric foundation connecting deformation to displacement fields and comprise normal and engineering shear strains.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-646c9364260cc8f0c76b71d04358c907&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2deea6eaa78cd0a482432f78f4310b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9a00e68fbbec347e4cd88332c5f0573</data>
