<node id="Schematic of 2D Infinitesimal Element Deformation and Strain (image)">
  <data key="d0">Schematic of 2D Infinitesimal Element Deformation and Strain (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram provides a visual representation of the strain state (Verzerrungszustand) for a two-dimensional infinitesimal element. It illustrates how displacement components (u, v) and their spatial gradients—derived via Taylor series expansion as discussed in the surrounding text—transform a square element into a deformed quadrilateral. The visualization explicitly links these displacement gradients to normal strains (changes in side length) and shear strains (changes in angles α, β, and γ_xy), serving as a fundamental model for continuum mechanics and elasticity theory.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-90cfec891927772de90cde9aa609de48</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784972310</data>
</node>
