</node>
<node id="Displacement Gradient Tensor">
  <data key="d0">Displacement Gradient Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tensor formed by the partial derivatives of displacement components, from which normal strains, shear strains, and rotations are computed.&lt;SEP&gt;A tensor derived from the linearization process, used to describe displacement gradients.&lt;SEP&gt;A tensor directly yielded by the linearized first-order approximation of the Taylor series expansion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-603ebcda3c395baf69674e7e06ddebff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39b2f0f24ccabd94f6101afe155c90b1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784998989</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
