<node id="Deformed Line Element Length under Small Deformation (Taylor Approximation) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Deformed Line Element Length under Small Deformation (Taylor Approximation) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation computes the deformed length P'Q' of an infinitesimal dx-element using a first-order Taylor approximation of the displacement field. The displacement u cancels, yielding P'Q' ≈ dx(1 + ∂u/∂x), where ∂u/∂x represents the normal strain. It is fundamental to deriving the infinitesimal strain tensor in linear continuum mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-978a28280c63d51b38f7e103fa1e1e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784972837</data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Strain Definition in x-Direction (Infinitesimal Strain) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Normal Strain Definition in x-Direction (Infinitesimal Strain) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Defines the normal strain ε_x as the partial derivative ∂u/∂x of the displacement field, derived from the relative elongation of a line element dx using first-order Taylor approximation. Foundational equation in linear continuum mechanics relating kinematic displacement to strain, underpinning stress analysis of deformable bodies.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784973332</data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Strain (ε_x)">
  <data key="d0">Normal Strain (ε_x)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Infinitesimal normal strain in the x-direction, central to the kinematics of deformation in continuum mechanics, computed as the relative elongation of an originally straight line segment and equal to the spatial gradient ∂u/∂x of the displacement component for small deformations</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999034</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Displacement Field (u)">
  <data key="d0">Displacement Field (u)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A position-dependent vector field whose spatial gradient, via a first-order Taylor expansion, yields the normal strain ε_x in the geometrically linear theory</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999034</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
