<node id="Small-Deformation Assumption">
  <data key="d0">Small-Deformation Assumption</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The geometrically linear theory assumption justifying the neglect of higher-order terms in the Taylor series expansion of the displacement field&lt;SEP&gt;The assumption that deformations are infinitesimally small, enabling simplifications such as tan(α) ≈ α and normal strains being negligible compared to 1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2deea6eaa78cd0a482432f78f4310b0</data>
