<node id="Tension Rods (Zugstäbe)">
  <data key="d0">Tension Rods (Zugstäbe)</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Load-bearing components in structural mechanics for which finite element analysis enables the calculation of stresses, strains, and deformations</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Page 4 - Introduction to Taylor Series in Strain Analysis (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Page 4 - Introduction to Taylor Series in Strain Analysis (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Page 4 of a continuum mechanics lecture introduces Taylorreihe (Taylor series) as power series for approximating functions at evaluation points. It covers 1D and multi-dimensional cases for small displacements, providing the mathematical foundation for analyzing strain states introduced in Section 12.1 Verzerrungszustand.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784973384</data>
</node>
<node id="Taylor Series">
  <data key="d0">Taylor Series</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A foundational mathematical tool (Taylorreihe) described as a power series used for approximating arbitrary functions at an evaluation/development point, essential for deriving strain tensors and displacement gradients in continuum mechanics.&lt;SEP&gt;The mathematical formulation of a function's expansion about an evaluation point, representing any sufficiently smooth function as an infinite sum of polynomial terms based on its derivatives at a single point.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical expansion used to find the displaced position of neighboring points, utilizing the reference state as the zeroth-order term.&lt;SEP&gt;A mathematical method serving as the foundational basis (from page 4) for the progression to small displacement considerations and multi-dimensional strain analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2baa9c55366fde92e0ba418495c7bae0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b5c4f815450e226a7f0b65824388cf</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Power Series">
  <data key="d0">Power Series</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical series representation (Potenzreihe); the Taylor series is categorized as a specific type of power series used for function approximation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Evaluation/Development Point">
  <data key="d0">Evaluation/Development Point</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The point (Auswertungs-/Entwicklungspunkt) at which arbitrary functions are approximated using Taylor series expansions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="1-Dimensional Case">
  <data key="d0">1-Dimensional Case</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific mathematical scenario evaluating small displacements (dℓ) at position ℓ, serving as the basis before extension to multiple dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Dimensional Case">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Dimensional Case</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An extension of the 1-dimensional mathematical scenario used for evaluating small displacements using Taylor series.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999045</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
