<node id="Page 9 - Mohr's Strain Circle and Spatial Deformation Introduction (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Page 9 - Mohr's Strain Circle and Spatial Deformation Introduction (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Page number '9' identifies the page introducing Mohr's strain circle (ε, γ/2) as an analogy to Mohr's stress circle (σ, τ), bridging 2D strain tensor theory with spatial (3D) deformation analysis. This page marks a key transition in section 12.1 Verzerrungszustand, extending plane strain concepts to three-dimensional states.</data>
