<node id="Three-Dimensional Displacement Vector Field Decomposition (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Three-Dimensional Displacement Vector Field Decomposition (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Decomposition of the 3D displacement vector field r(x,y,z) into Cartesian components u, v, w along unit vectors e_x, e_y, e_z. Serves as the kinematic foundation for deriving the strain tensor in three-dimensional deformation analysis, connecting displacement gradients to strains and subsequently to stresses via the elasticity law (Hooke's law) for homogeneous isotropic materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784979358</data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Dimensional Cartesian Coordinate System">
  <data key="d0">Three-Dimensional Cartesian Coordinate System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A coordinate system with orthogonal scalar components used to describe the position and displacement of material points in three dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Position Vector r(x,y,z)">
  <data key="d0">Position Vector r(x,y,z)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A vector that describes the displacement of a material point located at coordinates (x,y,z) within a deformable body.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cartesian Unit Vectors">
  <data key="d0">Cartesian Unit Vectors</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The orthogonal basis vectors (e_x, e_y, e_{z_i}) used to decompose the displacement vector into its respective scalar components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Dimensional Deformation State">
  <data key="d0">Three-Dimensional Deformation State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A spatial state of deformation (räumlicher Verformungszustand) analyzed using the displacement vector field and strain tensor.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999153</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poisson's Ratio ν">
  <data key="d0">Poisson's Ratio ν</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A material parameter (Querkontraktionszahl) used in constitutive laws to relate strains to stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;One of two independent material constants for isotropic elastic materials, used together with Young's modulus to derive the shear modulus via G = E / [2(1 + ν)].</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372d45ee57b3e8dd4b75b8ce18594fad</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U(x,y,z)">
  <data key="d0">U(x,y,z)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The scalar displacement component of the vector field in the x-direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-5f99bd9629698e210e8fd8be478fe64f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999158</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
