<node id="Page 10 - Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz Transition (page_number)">
  <data key="d0">Page 10 - Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz Transition (page_number)</data>
  <data key="d1">page_number</data>
  <data key="d2">Pagination marker '10' denoting the page where section 12.2 (Elastizitätsgesetz) begins. This page introduces Hooke's Law, material properties (homogeneous/isotropic), Poisson's ratio, and stress-strain relationships for plane stress conditions, following the strain state discussion from section 12.1.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784981514</data>
</node>
<node id="Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz">
  <data key="d0">Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz (Law of Elasticity or Hooke's Law) is a comprehensive section within a German-language mechanics and engineering document that covers foundational continuum mechanics concepts and elasticity theory. Initially introduced on page 10, the section's detailed content spans at least pages 13 through 15. It explores the fundamental constitutive laws and equations that govern linear elastic material behavior, incorporating key mechanical concepts such as the superposition principle.

A primary focus of Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz is the mechanical response of isotropic elastic materials, explicitly establishing that their behavior is defined by only two independent material constants. To demonstrate this, the section provides a detailed mathematical derivation of the relationship between the modulus of elasticity (Young's modulus) and the shear modulus. This derivation is conducted under plane stress conditions utilizing a biaxially loaded plate element, thereby illustrating the theoretical and mathematical relationships between various material moduli within the broader framework of Hooke's Law.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb63bc877af3e54e4e227db32248b763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a3421094c08152da74a60f04257a266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372d45ee57b3e8dd4b75b8ce18594fad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-235ab6bb09c88f34c57e39b028978709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47751b806b05c6d8ba7d4ccfae665886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec12900410ee6e1062ea25bf1aa27c44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef2929c1e9ff7a4d28ae04567e99b7f0</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
