  <data key="d5">1784999198</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poisson's Ratio (ν)">
  <data key="d0">Poisson's Ratio (ν)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A material parameter denoted by ν that quantifies transverse contraction. It is introduced on the page marked by page number 10 within Section 12.2.&lt;SEP&gt;An independent material constant for isotropic, elastic materials, to which G is mathematically correlated.&lt;SEP&gt;A material constant representing the ratio of transverse strain to axial strain in an elastic material.&lt;SEP&gt;A dimensionless material constant characterizing the transverse contraction per unit longitudinal extension.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Querdehnungszahl, a material property quantifying the Poisson effect as the ratio of transverse contraction to axial extension&lt;SEP&gt;A measure of the Poisson effect, which is the deformation of a material in directions perpendicular to the direction of loading, denoted by ν.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-004e08ca4afebf77525a1d7810f76686&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7377bf43fb474164c26372581df6f053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8f3f8c72a4f9a9fdeabe99c8c8ba4e</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999198</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
