<node id="Schematic of Uniaxial Tension and Lateral Contraction (image)">
  <data key="d0">Schematic of Uniaxial Tension and Lateral Contraction (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram visualizes the deformation of a rectangular material element subjected to uniaxial tensile stress ($\\sigma_x$) along the x-axis. It contrasts the original dimensions (black outline) with the deformed state (green area), illustrating longitudinal elongation and transverse contraction. This figure is central to explaining the Law of Elasticity and the concept of Poisson's ratio (Querkontraktionszahl) within the study of spatial strain states.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f11c25c44c43a5cf12c948c592916ad3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784981719</data>
</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law for Uniaxial Loading (Hookesches Gesetz) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law for Uniaxial Loading (Hookesches Gesetz) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation expresses the linear elastic constitutive relationship σ_x = E·ε_x for uniaxial loading, serving as the foundational basis for deriving the generalized plane stress elasticity law. It defines how normal stress produces proportional normal strain in homogeneous, isotropic materials, forming the starting point before incorporating Poisson's ratio effects and superposition for multiaxial stress states discussed in the surrounding context.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784982222</data>
</node>
