<node id="Transverse Strain Equation (Poisson Effect under Uniaxial Stress) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Transverse Strain Equation (Poisson Effect under Uniaxial Stress) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This constitutive equation describes the Poisson effect for isotropic materials under uniaxial stress, relating transverse strain ε_y to axial stress σ_x through Poisson's ratio ν and Young's modulus E. It demonstrates that plane stress produces three-dimensional strain, forming a fundamental component of the generalized Hooke's Law for the plane stress state analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784982456</data>
</node>
<node id="Transverse Strain">
  <data key="d0">Transverse Strain</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal strain in the y-direction resulting from loading in the perpendicular x-direction.&lt;SEP&gt;Strain in the perpendicular y-direction (ε_y = -ν·σ_x/E), negative due to the Poisson effect&lt;SEP&gt;The lateral deformation resulting from Poisson's effect.&lt;SEP&gt;The strain that results from two superposed effects: direct axial deformation due to σ_y and lateral contraction induced by σ_x through Poisson's effect.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as lateral contraction, it is the strain caused by normal stress in the perpendicular principal direction&lt;SEP&gt;The strain induced in transverse directions by transverse stresses, scaled by Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ce2fbc89309c5fa28f062356d8fd0dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7377bf43fb474164c26372581df6f053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f3dbcdc7efa91f1ffd56d0596ff25b</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poisson Effect">
  <data key="d0">Poisson Effect</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The Poisson Effect is a fundamental physical and mechanical phenomenon describing the transverse deformation of a material when it is subjected to loading in a perpendicular direction. Also referred to as *Querkontraktion* (lateral contraction), this effect explains how a material's strain in one principal direction is influenced by stress applied in orthogonal principal directions. Specifically, when tensile stress is applied uniaxially, it produces lateral contraction in the transverse directions. Conversely, the phenomenon also describes how a material tends to expand perpendicular to the direction of applied compression. 

This mechanical behavior is mathematically quantified by a material property known as Poisson's ratio ($\nu$). Within the framework of generalized Hooke's Law, the Poisson Effect is represented by negative coupling terms in the strain equations, such as $-\nu\cdot\sigma_y$. This negative sign mathematically captures the physical reality that an extension (tensile strain) in the direction of loading results in a proportional contraction in the orthogonal directions. 

For multi-axial states of stress, the lateral strain induced by stresses in orthogonal principal directions is captured by mathematical expressions that combine Poisson's ratio with the respective principal stresses, such as $\nu(\sigma_1 + \sigma_3)$ or $-\nu\cdot(\sigma_1 + \sigma_2)$. In a three-dimensional context, this means that transverse stresses (such as $\sigma_y$ and $\sigma_z$) will induce a transverse strain that is directly scaled by Poisson's ratio, fully defining the material's comprehensive deformation under load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804dc5da5931340fcffd232bf52ac41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7377bf43fb474164c26372581df6f053&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f3dbcdc7efa91f1ffd56d0596ff25b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95513f4440188d0181ac3f745cc0cfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650f3440dee3d2c3acd18a9d3ea4f7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-665c0dff808ce919d3762159ff91d81a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c347d0d02f605dcaeeba6088d212ddc8</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999263</data>
