<node id="Uniaxial Hooke's Law with Poisson Effect (σ_y Loading) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Uniaxial Hooke's Law with Poisson Effect (σ_y Loading) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Defines the longitudinal strain (ε_y) and transverse strain (ε_x) caused by a uniaxial normal stress σ_y in an isotropic elastic material under plane stress. Combines Hooke's Law (E) with Poisson's ratio (ν) to capture biaxial strain response, serving as a building block for the generalized plane stress constitutive equations via superposition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-bea3b0c0359c27ce74b4b9c1af45297a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784982778</data>
</node>
<node id="Hooke's Law for Plane Stress: x-Direction Strain Constitutive Equation (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Hooke's Law for Plane Stress: x-Direction Strain Constitutive Equation (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This constitutive equation from the generalized Hooke's Law describes normal strain ε_x under plane stress conditions (ESZ) for isotropic materials. It combines the direct axial strain (σ_x/E) with the Poisson-induced transverse strain (-νσ_y/E), embodying the superposition principle. It forms part of the compliance matrix formulation essential for structural analysis of thin-walled components.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784983285</data>
</node>
<node id="Principle Of Linear Superposition">
  <data key="d0">Principle Of Linear Superposition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A theory stating that the total strain state of a material results from the vectorial addition of individual stress contributions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Compliance Matrix Formulation">
  <data key="d0">Compliance Matrix Formulation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A full matrix representation of the linear elastic relationship between stress and strain vectors for plane stress conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Part I of Hooke's law expressing strains as functions of stresses, natural for displacement-controlled problems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4640da85a6d88df2121f23eab1d68369</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Computational Mechanics">
  <data key="d0">Computational Mechanics</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A discipline concerned with computational simulation and solving mechanical problems, utilizing stiffness matrices.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Three-Dimensional Hooke's Law">
  <data key="d0">Three-Dimensional Hooke's Law</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The generalized physical law for materials under a full three-dimensional state of stress, to which the plane stress equation connects.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constitutive Equation for Strain in y-direction under Plane Stress (Hooke's Law, ESZ) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Equation for Strain in y-direction under Plane Stress (Hooke's Law, ESZ) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation computes the normal strain ε_y in the y-direction under plane stress conditions for a homogeneous, isotropic material. It combines the direct strain from σ_y and the Poisson contraction from σ_x, using Young's modulus E and Poisson's ratio ν. It is part of the constitutive matrix for the plane stress state (ESZ).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784983413</data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Strain Equation $\varepsilon_y$">
  <data key="d0">Normal Strain Equation $\varepsilon_y$</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical equation representing one of the constitutive relations of Hooke's Law for a homogeneous, isotropic material under plane stress conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Strain $\varepsilon_y$">
  <data key="d0">Normal Strain $\varepsilon_y$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal strain in the y-direction, calculated as a superposition of direct longitudinal strain and transverse contraction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress $\sigma_y$">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress $\sigma_y$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal stress acting in the y-direction, producing direct longitudinal strain.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Transverse Contraction">
  <data key="d0">Transverse Contraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The contraction effect, or Querkontraktion, induced by normal stress acting perpendicular to the direction of interest.&lt;SEP&gt;The mechanical phenomenon accounted for by the term $-\frac{\nu}{E}(\sigma_z + \sigma_x)$, caused by orthogonal stresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95513f4440188d0181ac3f745cc0cfe1</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Normal Stress $\sigma_x$">
  <data key="d0">Normal Stress $\sigma_x$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal stress acting in the x-direction, inducing transverse contraction in the y-direction.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Poisson's Ratio $\nu$">
  <data key="d0">Poisson's Ratio $\nu$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An independent material constant for isotropic elastic materials that captures the Poisson effect.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Strain In The Z-direction $\varepsilon_z$">
  <data key="d0">Strain In The Z-direction $\varepsilon_z$</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A spatial strain arising in the z-direction, calculated as $-\nu/E \cdot (\sigma_x + \sigma_y)$, even when normal stress $\sigma_z$ equals zero.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Constitutive Matrix For Plane Stress">
  <data key="d0">Constitutive Matrix For Plane Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A full matrix formulation relating strains ($\varepsilon_x$, $\varepsilon_y$, $\gamma_{xy}$) to stresses ($\sigma_x$, $\sigma_y$, $\tau_{xy}$) in a plane stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999249</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Membrane Structures">
  <data key="d0">Membrane Structures</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
