<node id="Isotropic Elastic Materials">
  <data key="d0">Isotropic Elastic Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Materials characterized by having only two independent material constants (E and ν), representing a fundamental principle in material science.&lt;SEP&gt;A category of materials for which material constants are provided in the Elastizitätsgesetz chapter.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials with uniform elastic properties in all directions, whose characterization relies on the fundamental relationship between elastic constants.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials for which Hooke's law and thermal expansion are discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;Materials whose elastic properties are identical in all directions, where principal strain directions match principal stress directions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4a3421094c08152da74a60f04257a266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e13c1eccdbc66212f603ee56ccf63b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb6bcdf61d79257b9e57addd3e70b101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b8f3f8c72a4f9a9fdeabe99c8c8ba4e</data>
