<node id="Definition of the Shear Modulus (Schubmodul) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Definition of the Shear Modulus (Schubmodul) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Defines the shear modulus $G$ in units of $N/mm^2$. It represents a material's resistance to shear deformation under shear stress. While fundamental to the law of elasticity, it is mathematically dependent on Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio for isotropic materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784984671</data>
</node>
<node id="G (Shear Modulus)">
  <data key="d0">G (Shear Modulus)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A scalar material constant defined as 'Schubmodul', characterizing rigidity against shear deformation, and mathematically correlated to Young's Modulus and Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Newtons Per Square Millimeter [N/mm^2]">
  <data key="d0">Newtons Per Square Millimeter [N/mm^2]</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The physical unit of the shear modulus G, equivalent to Megapascals.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Deformation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Deformation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Denoted as gamma, it is induced by shear stresses and resisted by the rigidity characterized by G.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999272</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Torsion Tests">
  <data key="d0">Torsion Tests</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">An experimental method typically used to determine the value of the shear modulus G.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-4bc48465db9a039c612fe9cd175c5ccc</data>
