<node id="Relationship between Shear Modulus, Young's Modulus, and Poisson's Ratio (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Relationship between Shear Modulus, Young's Modulus, and Poisson's Ratio (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Fundamental constitutive identity for isotropic linear elastic materials relating shear modulus G to Young's modulus E and Poisson's ratio ν. Demonstrates that only two independent material constants govern isotropic elasticity, derived via biaxial loading analysis of a shear-loaded plate under plane stress conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784984779</data>
</node>
<node id="Shear Modulus Equation">
  <data key="d0">Shear Modulus Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An equation representing the fundamental constitutive relationship in linear isotropic elasticity theory, connecting shear modulus, Young's modulus, and Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
