<node id="Mohr's Circle for Pure Shear in Biaxial Loading (image)">
  <data key="d0">Mohr's Circle for Pure Shear in Biaxial Loading (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This image illustrates a Mohr's Circle centered at the origin, representing a state of pure shear stress equivalent to biaxial loading with principal stresses σ and -σ. The diagram demonstrates that the maximum shear stress τ is equal in magnitude to the normal stress σ. This visualization is essential for deriving the fundamental relationship between the elastic constants E (Young's modulus) and G (shear modulus) for isotropic materials, as described in the accompanying text on elasticity laws.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784985257</data>
</node>
<node id="Law Of Elasticity">
  <data key="d0">Law Of Elasticity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Also known as Elastizitätsgesetz, discussed in the surrounding content related to the derivation of moduli relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;Also known as Elastizitätsgesetz, it is the theoretical framework surrounding the derivation of relationships between elastic constants.&lt;SEP&gt;A broader discussion, referred to as 'Elastizitätsgesetz', bridging basic uniaxial stress to full tensorial representation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5804dc5da5931340fcffd232bf52ac41</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999279</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
