<node id="Geometric Deformation Diagram for Elastic Moduli Derivation (image)">
  <data key="d0">Geometric Deformation Diagram for Elastic Moduli Derivation (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram depicts the transformation of a square material element into a rhombus under biaxial stress, serving as a visual proof for the relationship between Young's modulus and shear modulus. By quantifying the change in length ($l - \Delta l$) and the resulting angular distortion ($\gamma$), the illustration facilitates the mathematical derivation of the elasticity law for isotropic materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2b68662a379adb00139d0404ab69c20e</data>
