<node id="Equivalent Stress Design Criterion (Vergleichsspannungsnachweis) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Stress Design Criterion (Vergleichsspannungsnachweis) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This inequality σ_V ≤ σ_zul is the central design verification equation in strength of materials. It requires that the scalar equivalent stress (Vergleichsspannung), derived from a multi-axial stress state via a strength hypothesis, does not exceed the admissible stress determined from uniaxial material testing. It connects theoretical stress analysis with practical structural safety assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-343794ade2b1d656c68e2c17454713f5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784992239</data>
</node>
<node id="Stress Verification Equation">
  <data key="d0">Stress Verification Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A fundamental structural design criterion ($\sigma_V \leq \sigma_{zul}$) representing a sufficient condition for structural safety in the strength of materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-343794ade2b1d656c68e2c17454713f5</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999464</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
