</node>
<node id="Uniaxial Equivalent Stress Calibration Condition (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Uniaxial Equivalent Stress Calibration Condition (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">Defines the boundary conditions of a uniaxial tensile test ($\sigma_1 = \sigma_V, \sigma_2 = \sigma_3 = 0$). It is used to calibrate and derive the equivalent stress formula for the distortion energy hypothesis, allowing complex 3D stress states to be compared to simple material yield limits.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784993533</data>
</node>
<node id="Equation (σ1 = σV &amp; σ2 = 0)">
  <data key="d0">Equation (σ1 = σV &amp; σ2 = 0)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A mathematical representation establishing boundary conditions for a uniaxial stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uniaxial Stress State">
  <data key="d0">Uniaxial Stress State</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A one-dimensional tensile load condition used to mathematically calibrate equivalent stress.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Stress (σV)">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Stress (σV)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A single scalar value used to compare complex multi-axial stress states against material yield strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Principal Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d0">Principal Stress Tensor</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A tensor describing the state of stress, which simplifies under a one-dimensional tensile load.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Maximum Principal Stress (σ1)">
  <data key="d0">Maximum Principal Stress (σ1)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The highest principal normal stress, set equal to the equivalent stress in a uniaxial condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999477</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Principal Stresses (σ2, σ3)">
  <data key="d0">Principal Stresses (σ2, σ3)</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The normal stresses acting perpendicular to principal planes, defined as zero in a uniaxial stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-808053be7d7f2ab70eb24b63ee8e1f52</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
