<node id="Crystal Lattice Deformation Diagram under Shear Stress (image)">
  <data key="d0">Crystal Lattice Deformation Diagram under Shear Stress (image)</data>
  <data key="d1">image</data>
  <data key="d2">This diagram provides a microscopic visualization of material deformation mechanisms under shear stress ($	au$). It contrasts an ideal crystal lattice with its state during elastic deformation (skewing) and elastic-plastic deformation (slip/displacement). This serves as a fundamental visual aid for the 'Schubspannungshypothese' (Shear Stress Hypothesis) discussed in the surrounding text, explaining how maximum shear stress leads to material loading and eventual failure through internal structural changes.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fe71d7fb091b493303186868a143418</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784993793</data>
</node>
<node id="38236c4d26554e7f90fb409f8f8ff2cef154fb4f64ba2b22d252eefaf378fb2a.jpg">
  <data key="d0">38236c4d26554e7f90fb409f8f8ff2cef154fb4f64ba2b22d252eefaf378fb2a.jpg</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A schematic diagram illustrating the microscopic behavior of a crystal lattice under shear stress, presented in three distinct stages.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fe71d7fb091b493303186868a143418</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
