</node>
<node id="Undeformierter Kristall">
  <data key="d0">Undeformierter Kristall</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The initial stage of the crystal lattice, shown as a regular, undeformed 5x6 grid of atoms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fe71d7fb091b493303186868a143418</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastische Verformung">
  <data key="d0">Elastische Verformung</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The second stage showing the lattice skewing into a parallelogram shape under shear stress while maintaining the continuity of all bonds, representing reversible bond stretching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fe71d7fb091b493303186868a143418</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999485</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Elastische/plastische Verformung">
  <data key="d0">Elastische/plastische Verformung</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The third stage showing further distortion and a visible horizontal displacement or 'slip', representing irreversible atomic sliding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-8fe71d7fb091b493303186868a143418</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999485</data>
