<node id="Von Mises Equivalent Stress Equation (Distortion Energy Hypothesis) (equation)">
  <data key="d0">Von Mises Equivalent Stress Equation (Distortion Energy Hypothesis) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d1">equation</data>
  <data key="d2">This equation defines the equivalent stress ($\sigma_v$) based on the principal stresses ($\sigma_1, \sigma_2, \sigma_3$) according to the distortion energy theory. It is used to predict yielding in ductile materials under multi-axial loading by comparing the deformation energy to a uniaxial stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-192ac0f71348510b81fe5091648ee0bb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784997342</data>
</node>
<node id="Principal Stress Formulation">
  <data key="d0">Principal Stress Formulation</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">The mathematical equation provided in the text, which calculates the equivalent uniaxial stress using the differences between principal stresses.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-192ac0f71348510b81fe5091648ee0bb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equivalent Uniaxial Stress">
  <data key="d0">Equivalent Uniaxial Stress</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented by the variable $\sigma_v$, it is the calculated stress value representing a general three-dimensional stress state equated to a uniaxial tensile stress state.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-192ac0f71348510b81fe5091648ee0bb</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Second Deviatoric Stress Invariant">
  <data key="d0">Second Deviatoric Stress Invariant</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Represented by $J_2$, this mathematical invariant is used to derive the von Mises yield criterion equation by taking its square roots.&lt;SEP&gt;A stress invariant that, upon reaching a critical value, triggers yielding according to the von Mises yield criterion.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-192ac0f71348510b81fe5091648ee0bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d00610e182d45a94eb2e712fcaa111a3</data>
  <data key="d4">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1784999493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
