  <data key="d13">1784999853</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastizitätsgesetz" target="l + Δl">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The expression l + Δl is fundamental to the derivation of the Elastizitätsgesetz.</data>
  <data key="d10">fundamental to derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999858</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastizitätsgesetz" target="Technical Schematic Diagram">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The technical schematic diagram serves as a geometric basis for the context of Elastizitätsgesetz.</data>
  <data key="d10">basis,context</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f286bbba14a03f81052794f20378e5cc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999866</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastizitätsgesetz" target="Shear Modulus (Schubmodul)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Elastizitätsgesetz derivation uses the relationship connecting shear modulus with Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio as a key step.</data>
  <data key="d10">constitutive law,derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastizitätsgesetz" target="Young's Modulus (E-Modul)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Young's modulus is incorporated into the Elastizitätsgesetz derivation through the fundamental elastic relationship G = E/[2(1+ν)].</data>
  <data key="d10">constitutive law,derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastizitätsgesetz" target="Fundamental Elastic Relationship">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The fundamental elastic relationship serves as a key step in the derivation of the Elastizitätsgesetz.</data>
  <data key="d10">derivation,key step</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f132449988465ad1aa01eccbc48da1a0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
