<edge source="Axial Stiffness" target="Young's Modulus">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Young's modulus is a component in calculating the axial stiffness (EA).&lt;SEP&gt;Axial stiffness is calculated as the product of Young's modulus and cross-sectional area.&lt;SEP&gt;Axial stiffness is the product of Young's modulus E and cross-sectional area A.&lt;SEP&gt;Axial Stiffness is mathematically calculated using the Young's Modulus.</data>
