<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Poisson's Ratio">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio governs the lateral contraction induced by the normal stress in multiaxial stress states.</data>
  <data key="d10">governs,lateral contraction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Lateral Contraction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In multiaxial stress states, normal stress additionally induces lateral contraction.</data>
  <data key="d10">induces</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Axial Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Axial strain is directly related to normal stress through the one-dimensional Hooke's Law relationship.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculated,related</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999794</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Longitudinal Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Longitudinal strain is directly proportional to normal stress via ε_x = σ_x/E</data>
  <data key="d10">equation,proportionality</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999812</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Transverse Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Transverse strain is related to normal stress via ε_y = -ν·σ_x/E</data>
  <data key="d10">equation,proportionality</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999812</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Normal Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Normal strain in a given direction is calculated as a function of the normal stress applied in that and the perpendicular direction.</data>
  <data key="d10">function of,induced by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999841</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Strain Component Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The strain component equation uses the normal stress quantity sigma to compute the normal strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculates,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b5deab09d1c9d30fa6463bb3156b4278</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999861</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress" target="Hooke's Constitutive Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Normal stress σ is a key variable in Hooke's constitutive equation ε = σ/E × (1 + ν).</data>
  <data key="d10">constitutive law,variable</data>
