<edge source="Strain" target="Stress">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The document content transitions from discussing Stress to introducing Strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress (dynamic quantities) is distinguished from strain (kinematic quantities).&lt;SEP&gt;The equation establishes that strain is directly proportional to applied stress, with Young's modulus serving as the inverse scaling factor.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress and Strain are covered together in a summary section of the document preceding page 27.</data>
  <data key="d10">directly proportional,distinct from,related concepts,summarized together,transition to</data>
