<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Young's Modulus">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's Law uses Young's Modulus as its proportionality factor relating stress to strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Hooke's Law governs linear-elastic behavior with Young's modulus E as the proportionality constant.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus (E) is a material property parameter used in Hooke's Law for axial loading&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus E is a key parameter in Hooke's Law relating mechanical elongation to applied force.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus is a parameter used in Hooke's law to calculate elastic shortenings.</data>
