<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Normal Strain (ε_x)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal strain measure ε_x is essential for the constitutive law known as Hooke's law</data>
  <data key="d10">essential for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0deb8f7c8c663233e195e68e3b5afeea</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999721</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Structural Engineering">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Structural engineering uses Hooke's Law to calculate stresses based on derived strain quantities.</data>
  <data key="d10">application,stress analysis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Material Science">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Material science applies Hooke's Law to predict material failure based on evaluated strains.</data>
  <data key="d10">application,failure prediction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Elasticity Law">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Elasticity Law combines the shear constitutive relationship with Hooke's law for normal components to form a complete linear elastic material model.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination,includes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999785</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Young's Modulus E">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's law relates normal stress σ to normal strain ε via Young's modulus E (σ = E · ε).</data>
  <data key="d10">material property,proportional relationship</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999785</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Normal Stress σ">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's law defines the relationship between normal stress and normal strain for linear elastic materials.</data>
  <data key="d10">constitutive relationship,stress component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999785</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Normal Strain ε">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's law defines the relationship between normal strain and normal stress for linear elastic materials.</data>
  <data key="d10">constitutive relationship,strain component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b83a395393ea0f85f23d45221be850ae</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999785</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Page Number 10">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The page marked by page number 10 introduces Hooke's Law (σ = E⋅ε) as a foundational concept.</data>
  <data key="d10">introduces</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999790</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Linear Elasticity Theory">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's Law (σ = E⋅ε) is a foundational element of linear elasticity theory, relating stress and strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Hooke's Law provides the framework for the constitutive relationship within linear elasticity theory</data>
  <data key="d10">basis,belongs to,foundational to,framework</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999790</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz">
  <data key="d8">5.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Section 12.2 covers foundational continuum mechanics concepts including Hooke's Law.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz presents Hooke's law generalized for plane stress conditions as a fundamental constitutive law.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 12.2 'Elastizitätsgesetz' is directly translated as Hooke's Law or Law of Elasticity.&lt;SEP&gt;Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz is directly translated to and concerns Hooke's Law (Elasticity Law).&lt;SEP&gt;Section 12.2 Elastizitätsgesetz translates to Elasticity Law, which is also known as Hooke's Law.</data>
  <data key="d10">also known as,contains,covers,equivalent to,presents,translated as</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb63bc877af3e54e4e227db32248b763&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a3421094c08152da74a60f04257a266&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47751b806b05c6d8ba7d4ccfae665886&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec12900410ee6e1062ea25bf1aa27c44</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999791</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Elastic Modulus (E)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's Law (σ = E⋅ε) uses the elastic modulus (E) as the proportionality constant relating stress and strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">incorporates,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-64914dffaa71b279b32225287f51b6fd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999791</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="ε_x = σ_x / E">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation ε_x = σ_x / E represents the fundamental uniaxial form of Hooke's Law.</data>
  <data key="d10">represents,uniaxial form</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999792</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Normal Strain">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's Law establishes a linear constitutive relationship involving normal strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Hooke's Law for biaxial stress is used to determine the normal strain (ε) based on applied stress and material properties.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculates,determines,establishes relationship,linear constitutive</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55f0f77e6766d722b567e55f8b17701c</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Plane Stress State">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The generalized elasticity law for the plane stress state is derived using the equation as a foundational building block.&lt;SEP&gt;Hooke's law is generalized for plane stress conditions under homogeneous and isotropic material assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to,building block,derives from,generalized for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb63bc877af3e54e4e227db32248b763</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Principle Of Superposition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The principle of superposition extends the uniaxial relationship to account for multiaxial stress states.</data>
  <data key="d10">extends,multiaxial</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Homogeneous Isotropic Elastic Materials">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's Law establishes a linear constitutive relationship for homogeneous, isotropic elastic materials.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4512fdc0f661bddfaf9a4f9bea1eef2f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999793</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Homogeneous And Isotropic Material Assumptions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's law is generalized for plane stress conditions under homogeneous and isotropic material assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d10">assumes,relies on</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cb63bc877af3e54e4e227db32248b763</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999796</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Elastic Material Behavior">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's law serves as a fundamental constitutive law governing elastic material behavior.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to,governs</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-cb63bc877af3e54e4e227db32248b763</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999796</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Law" target="Stress and Strain Tensors">
