<edge source="Young's Modulus" target="Poisson's Ratio">
  <data key="d8">4.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio are equivalent to the Lamé parameters for isotropic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's Modulus and Poisson's ratio jointly define the constitutive relationship that links Young's Modulus to Shear Modulus in linear elasticity theory.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio are interdependent isotropic elastic material constants.&lt;SEP&gt;Young's modulus is mathematically related to the shear modulus and Poisson's ratio via the formula G = E / [2(1+ν)].</data>
