<edge source="Technische Mechanik 2" target="Continuum Mechanics">
  <data key="d8">12.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relation "(Continuum Mechanics, Technische Mechanik 2)" establishes that the content of the textbook "Technische Mechanik 2" is situated entirely within the academic field of continuum mechanics. This relationship highlights the textbook as an educational resource fundamentally focused on this specific domain of engineering and physics.

Within this context, "Technische Mechanik 2" covers the fundamental concepts of continuum mechanics to provide readers with the necessary baseline knowledge. The textbook is specifically utilized to facilitate a deeper exploration and advanced study of the subject matter. The instructional focus of the book particularly emphasizes stress analysis, offering detailed coverage of critical mechanical phenomena. To thoroughly explain these principles, the text explores key topics including stress vectors, stress tensors, normal stresses, and shear stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;The textbook Technische Mechanik 2 provides academic provenance for complex continuum mechanics concepts.&lt;SEP&gt;The textbook Technische Mechanik 2 serves as the literature origin for the continuum mechanics concepts discussed.&lt;SEP&gt;The textbook 'Technische Mechanik 2' is a standard reference for continuum mechanics.&lt;SEP&gt;The textbook provides an academic basis and grounding for continuum mechanics concepts.</data>
