</edge>
<edge source="Straight Bar" target="Uniform Stress Distribution">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The assumption of uniform stress distribution is valid for bars with constant or weakly varying cross-sectional areas.</data>
  <data key="d10">applicability,valid for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Straight Bar" target="Method of Sections">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The method of sections is applied to straight bars to determine internal normal forces by making a cut perpendicular to the bar axis.</data>
  <data key="d10">analysis,applied to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Straight Bar" target="Tension/Compression Members">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The elementary theory of tension/compression members describes the behavior of straight bars under axial loading.</data>
  <data key="d10">describes,theory</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-61bee0456fb356f553c6809b0f9fb7ef</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
