  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Constitutive Relation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing ODE is derived by substituting the constitutive relation N = E·A·(u' - α_T·ΔT) into the equilibrium condition.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from,substitution</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Distributed Axial Load">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The right-hand side of the ODE contains the distributed line load n representing self-weight.</data>
  <data key="d10">contains term</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Temperature Change">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The right-hand side of the ODE contains the derivative of the thermal term involving ΔT.</data>
  <data key="d10">contains term</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Finite Element Formulation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing ODE is central to the finite element formulation for bar elements.</data>
  <data key="d10">central to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Hanging Bar Under Self-Weight">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing ODE is applied to the hanging bar under self-weight, a statically determinate problem.</data>
  <data key="d10">applied to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Single Rod">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing second-order ordinary differential equation describes the axial displacement of a single rod or bar.</data>
  <data key="d10">applied to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Kinematic Relation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing ODE is derived by combining the kinematic relation ε = u'(x) with the equilibrium condition and Hooke's law</data>
  <data key="d10">derived_from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Axial Displacement Field">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing ODE describes the axial displacement field u(x) of a one-dimensional structural member under distributed axial load</data>
  <data key="d10">describes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Line Load">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The line load n appears on the right-hand side of the governing ODE as the constant distributed axial load</data>
  <data key="d10">load_term</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Boundary Value Problem">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Boundary conditions u(0) = 0 and u'(l) = 0 complete the boundary value problem for the governing ODE</data>
  <data key="d10">completes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="One-Dimensional Structural Member">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The one-dimensional structural member (rod/bar) is the physical system whose axial displacement is governed by the ODE</data>
  <data key="d10">analyzed_by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Governing ODE For Axial Displacement" target="Displacement Solution">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement solution u(x) = (1/EA)(-n/2·x² + G·x) is obtained by integrating the governing ODE</data>
  <data key="d10">derived_from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Longitudinal Strain Field">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The longitudinal strain field is defined as the first-order spatial derivative of the axial displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">definition,derivative</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Lagrangian Coordinate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The axial displacement field measures the longitudinal displacement with respect to the Lagrangian coordinate.</data>
  <data key="d10">domain,measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Derivative Operator">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The derivative operator is applied to the axial displacement field to calculate the local gradient, provided the field is at least once differentiable.</data>
  <data key="d10">application,differentiation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-635877c2ca4bd8652a8de3e6ef23d5f9</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Axial Displacement Field" target="Axial Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Axial strain is defined as the first derivative of the axial displacement field with respect to position.</data>
  <data key="d10">derivative,kinematics</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-794d30f8b956a266f2b6d66cc7f678de</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distributed Axial Load" target="Self-Weight">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The distributed axial load n represents the self-weight of the structure in this specific context.</data>
  <data key="d10">represents</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distributed Axial Load" target="Infinitesimal Element">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The distributed axial load acts over the infinitesimal length of the element, with a resultant of n·dx.</data>
  <data key="d10">acts over</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-45f0f3e4c4e1775f77972c4268710cbb</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897131</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Coefficient Of Thermal Expansion" target="Constitutive Relation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The constitutive relation incorporates the coefficient of thermal expansion α_T to account for thermal strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">incorporates</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c97b092fc202625d8ee8acd1894cf787</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Coefficient Of Thermal Expansion" target="Governing Differential Equation E·A·u''(x) + n(x) − E·A·α·ΔT' = 0">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The governing differential equation incorporates the coefficient of thermal expansion α as a material property parameter.</data>
  <data key="d10">contains,parameter</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Coefficient Of Thermal Expansion" target="Segment 1">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The coefficient of thermal expansion (αT) determines the thermal strain in Segment 1 when temperature change ΔT is applied</data>
