  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="n" target="Hanging Bar">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The distributed load n arises from the self-weight of the hanging bar.</data>
  <data key="d10">source of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b5cc011b4f71d9c304cbdecd2839b81e</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="n" target="Einzelstab">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Einzelstab is subjected to a constant distributed load denoted by the variable n.</data>
  <data key="d10">distributed load,parameter</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="n" target="Distributed Line Load">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">n represents the distributed line load (Linienkraft) measured in force per unit length [N/m]</data>
  <data key="d10">physical quantity,represents</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="n" target="Uniform Loading">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">When n is constant along the bar length, it represents uniform loading, allowing simplification of the distributed load integral to n·l</data>
  <data key="d10">loading condition,special case of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-faaf238bf3e3a6116edca46159e939df</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897132</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="G" target="Line Load">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">G is related to the constant line load through n = G/l, where l is the bar length, representing total self-weight divided by length</data>
  <data key="d10">related_to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897128</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="G" target="Bar Length">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">G and bar length l are related through n = G/l, defining the line load as self-weight per unit length</data>
  <data key="d10">related_to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f4f759f99f5a784630c625df026ca993</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="G" target="Einzelstab">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total weight or self-load of the Einzelstab is signified by the variable G.</data>
  <data key="d10">load,weight</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-17b87724a453e2805522671a76c088ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="G" target="C₁">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The integration constant C₁, derived from boundary conditions u(x=0)=0 and u'(x=l)=0, equals G.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from,equals</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-213cdd3f8f32396583dc5a4fa4d54dfd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="G" target="σ_max">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
