</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Three-bar System">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The kinematic compatibility condition is required to solve the statically indeterminate three-bar system because equilibrium conditions alone are insufficient.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to,constrains</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Bar Forces">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Combined with equilibrium conditions and Hooke's law, the kinematic compatibility condition allows the determination of all unknown bar forces.</data>
  <data key="d10">determines,solves for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f72457639c5767731980d0c54a4fe069</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Statically Indeterminate Rod">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The compatibility condition describes the total axial deformation constraint for the statically indeterminate doubly clamped rod.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to,describes</data>
