  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897131</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Thermal Expansion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The free thermal expansion term is a component of the compatibility equation that is exactly offset by mechanical strains.</data>
  <data key="d10">component of,offset by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897131</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Superposition Method">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The superposition method parallels the compatibility condition approach by canceling thermal displacement with mechanical displacement.</data>
  <data key="d10">parallels,relates to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-abc3cadf3a789dbb882aa778366ab3b3</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897131</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Kinematic Compatibility Condition" target="Boundary Condition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The kinematic compatibility condition is the explicit mathematical evaluation of the boundary condition Δl = Δl_1 + Δl_2 = 0 for the doubly clamped rod.</data>
