<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Normal Force (Normalkraft)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal stress σ(x) is defined as the quotient of the normal force N(x) divided by the cross-sectional area</data>
  <data key="d10">defined by,quotient of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Cross-sectional Area (Querschnittsfläche)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal stress σ(x) is calculated by dividing the normal force by the cross-sectional area A(x), which may vary along the bar's longitudinal axis</data>
  <data key="d10">defined by,divided by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Cauchy's Stress Theory">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation for normal stress is rooted in Cauchy's stress theory as its theoretical foundation</data>
  <data key="d10">based on,rooted in</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Cross-section Dimensioning (Querschnittsbemessung)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Cross-section dimensioning applies the normal stress formula, rearranged as A_erf = |N|/σ_zul, to determine the minimum required cross-sectional area</data>
  <data key="d10">applies,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Stress Concentrations (Spannungsspitzen)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Stress concentrations produce non-uniform distributions that cannot be captured by the elementary normal stress formula, representing a key limitation of the theory near discontinuities</data>
  <data key="d10">limitation of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Tension Member (Zugstab)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">For a tension member, a positive normal force N(x) &gt; 0 produces positive tensile stress σ &gt; 0</data>
  <data key="d10">positive,produces</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Stress (Normalspannung)" target="Compression Member (Druckstab)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">For a compression member, a negative normal force N(x) &lt; 0 yields negative compressive stress σ &lt; 0</data>
  <data key="d10">negative,produces</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e52c13f9f7327cff72c363dce5291e4</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897129</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
