</edge>
<edge source="Elongation Equation Δl = u(l) − u(0)" target="Fundamental Theorem Of Calculus">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The elongation equation is obtained by applying the fundamental theorem of calculus to the integral of the strain field.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived using,proven by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784897130</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elongation Equation Δl = u(l) − u(0)" target="Statically Determinate Hanging Rod">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The elongation equation is employed in the analysis of statically determinate hanging rods under self-weight, where u(0) = 0 yields Δl = u(l).</data>
  <data key="d10">applied to,used in</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0963d089a81497869e206f806e6e66d1</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel10_Elastostatik_Zug_und_Druck_in_Stäben.pdf</data>
