  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio (ν) is a parameter in the generalized Hooke's Law equation, used to account for the lateral contraction or expansion due to perpendicular stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The generalized Hooke's Law equation uses Poisson's ratio ν to account for transverse strain effects.</data>
