<edge source="Cauchy Stress Tensor" target="Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The stress tensor concept culminates in the Cauchy stress tensor, which completely characterizes the internal force distribution at any point.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cauchy stress tensor σ is the standard notation representing the symmetric stress tensor in continuum mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d10">characterization,is a specific type of,synonym</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7876e6fbf1af5b17253567ec9af4cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-012508b359d5f14b7a687dd269f97c12</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904218</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Cauchy Stress Tensor" target="Point P">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Cauchy stress tensor provides the complete stress state description at point P across all possible cutting planes.&lt;SEP&gt;The symmetry property of the Cauchy stress tensor is derived using moment equilibrium conditions about coordinate axes passing through Point P.</data>
  <data key="d10">definition,derived from,equilibrium condition,pointwise</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7876e6fbf1af5b17253567ec9af4cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cabab253ce4ee75c98c51cfd7f1a27b</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904218</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
