<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Normal Strain Component ε_x">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal strain characterizes deformation behavior together with transverse strains governed by Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d10">associated with,characterizes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-88f6cb959dc0f4ce6e1902a94dcb7d12</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999781</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Hooke's Generalized Law">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Hooke's generalized law uses Poisson's ratio as a material constant.</data>
  <data key="d10">depends on,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b37ac6d222ba4898f7b2f8f457e77e5d</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999783</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Material Constants">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio is a specific type of material constant used in the elasticity law.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's Ratio is one of the three Material Constants connected by the Shear Modulus Equation.</data>
  <data key="d10">example of,includes,is a</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b37ac6d222ba4898f7b2f8f457e77e5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999783</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Transverse Strain">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio is the proportionality constant that determines the magnitude of transverse contraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio quantifies the lateral contraction in transverse strain via ε_y = -ν·σ_x/E</data>
  <data key="d10">equation,governs,parameter,quantification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b73317ca6218a3794fd92d7cfec3e4db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999794</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Shear Modulus">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Shear modulus G depends on Poisson's ratio ν through the formula G = E/[2(1+ν)]&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio (ν) and Shear Modulus (G) are mathematically interdependent elastic material properties, with their relationship derivable from strain transformations and shear deformations.&lt;SEP&gt;The shear modulus is mathematically related to Young's modulus and Poisson's ratio via the formula G = E / [2(1+ν)].&lt;SEP&gt;The Shear Modulus is isolated and derived in terms of Poisson's ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shear Modulus is defined by the rational term utilizing Young's Modulus and Poisson's ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear Modulus is mathematically related to Young's Modulus and Poisson's ratio by the formula G = E/(2(1+ν)).</data>
  <data key="d10">calculated,dependency,derivable,derived from,formula,interdependent,mathematical relationship,related to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-926a4442fa510b596bda13f5de11afb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-963728870ca7c1f5d880eae3e1e47f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718443b278fc05d9b29615dd32329bd6</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999840</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Isotropic Elastic Behavior">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio is one of two independent constants required to fully characterize isotropic elastic behavior</data>
  <data key="d10">characterization,material constant</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999841</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Stress and Strain Tensors">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's ratio acts as a dimensionless proportionality constant establishing the linear homogeneous relationship between stress and strain tensors</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical operation,proportionality</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9d473000f8b85e21224cdb4fbff1c039</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999841</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Poisson Effect">
  <data key="d8">7.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The magnitude of the Poson effect, or lateral contraction, is quantified by the material's Poisson's ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;The Poisson effect is scaled by Poisson's ratio ν, determining the magnitude of transverse strain.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio is the material property that accounts for the Poisson effect caused by orthogonal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio quantifies the Poisson effect, which causes lateral contraction or expansion due to transverse stresses&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio ν mathematically quantifies the Poisson effect, representing transverse deformation caused by orthogonal stresses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Poisson effect is mathematically captured by terms involving Poisson's ratio.&lt;SEP&gt;Poisson's ratio is a dimensionless material property that represents the Poisson effect.</data>
  <data key="d10">captured by,characterizes,depends on,governs,quantified by,quantifies,represents,scaled by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6f3dbcdc7efa91f1ffd56d0596ff25b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95513f4440188d0181ac3f745cc0cfe1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-650f3440dee3d2c3acd18a9d3ea4f7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-665c0dff808ce919d3762159ff91d81a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c347d0d02f605dcaeeba6088d212ddc8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999842</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Shear Modulus Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Shear Modulus Equation connects Poisson's Ratio with Shear Modulus and Young's Modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">connects,defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999850</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Poisson Coupling Effect">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Poisson's Ratio captures the Poisson Coupling Effect between orthogonal directions.</data>
  <data key="d10">captures</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999851</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="G = E/[2(1+ν)]">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The derived formula mathematically relates the shear modulus to Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d10">relates to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999859</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson's Ratio" target="Strain Component Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The strain component equation incorporates Poisson's ratio ν, which describes transverse contraction under longitudinal loading and contributes the Poisson-induced lateral effect -νσ.</data>
  <data key="d10">depends on,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b5deab09d1c9d30fa6463bb3156b4278</data>
