<edge source="Stress Vector" target="Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d8">7.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Individual stress vectors are arranged into the stress tensor (matrix) to form its components&lt;SEP&gt;The stress vector concept leads to the stress tensor concept because stress at a point cannot be fully described by a single vector and requires the complete stress state across all cutting planes.&lt;SEP&gt;The insufficiency of a single stress vector to fully describe the stress state at a point directly motivates the need for the stress tensor concept&lt;SEP&gt;Stress vectors and stress tensors are discussed together in Section 11.1 of the technical mechanics content for the description of stress states.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress vector definition leads systematically to the tensor formulation of stress states.&lt;SEP&gt;Stress tensor components are derived from three stress vectors on mutually perpendicular sectional planes.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress tensor derivation began with the introduction of stress vectors on cutting planes, maintaining a continuous theoretical flow.</data>
  <data key="d10">arranged into,component of,components,derived from,foundation,foundation of,leads to,motivates,precedes,related concept,transition</data>
  <data key="d11">doc-ba92f82e2b057ed886fb58574a01ea0a-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84aaf5f754cbb16f87120d0c3bf0cd2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-271a171e393b79c95418cb0645e75d72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7876e6fbf1af5b17253567ec9af4cf91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60e545266c1919041c313cfba39a94c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cabab253ce4ee75c98c51cfd7f1a27b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ffd7059b21365543021b6e1a5ac8087</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904165</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
