<edge source="Stress Tensor" target="Shear Stress">
  <data key="d8">6.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The shear stresses form all remaining off-diagonal components of the stress tensor&lt;SEP&gt;Shear stress is a component of the stress state described by the stress tensor.&lt;SEP&gt;Shear stress components tau_xy, tau_xz, tau_yx, tau_yz, tau_zx, and tau_zy are integral parts of the stress tensor acting on the three positive faces of the volume element&lt;SEP&gt;The stress tensor contains shear stresses that reduce to three independent components due to symmetry relationships.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress tensor is symmetric, meaning shear stresses satisfy the condition τxy = τyx.&lt;SEP&gt;The stress tensor includes the shear stress component $\tau_{xy}$.</data>
  <data key="d10">component,components,composition,consists of,contains,has components,off-diagonal,symmetry,symmetry property</data>
