<edge source="Plane Stress State" target="Principal Stresses">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The longitudinal and circumferential principal stresses form the plane stress state (ESZ) in the vessel wall, as no shear stresses occur.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal stresses σ_x and σ_φ arise under the assumption of plane stress state (ebener Spannungszustand, ESZ) in thin-walled vessels.</data>
