<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Mohr's Circle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Under the hydrostatic stress state, Mohr's circle degenerates to a single point at (σ_0, 0) with a radius of zero.</data>
  <data key="d10">degeneration,geometric interpretation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Deviatoric Stress Decomposition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The hydrostatic stress state acts as the volumetric component that separates from the distortional component during deviatoric stress decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d10">component,separation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Sonderfall 1">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Unlike uniaxial tension (Sonderfall 1), the hydrostatic stress state produces no distortion.</data>
  <data key="d10">comparison,contrast</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Sonderfall 2">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Unlike pure shear (Sonderfall 2), the hydrostatic stress state produces no distortion.</data>
  <data key="d10">comparison,contrast</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904224</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Principal Stresses">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">In the hydrostatic stress state, the principal stresses are degenerate with σ_1 = σ_2 = σ_0, making every direction a principal direction.&lt;SEP&gt;The hydrostatic stress state equates the three principal stresses to a single scalar value.</data>
  <data key="d10">degenerate,equates,mathematical property</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a30bb490f8e8f9e0d00884e4cba69c8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf&lt;SEP&gt;Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999880</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Maximum Shear Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The maximum shear stress equals zero in the hydrostatic stress state regardless of orientation.</data>
  <data key="d10">physical property,zero</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0d8ef0753f64ed72eb451c29b8108d08</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904225</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Stress State" target="Stress Invariants">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
