  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Principal Stresses" target="Equivalent Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The squared differences between principal stresses ($\sigma_1$, $\sigma_2$, $\sigma_3$) are scaled by a coefficient to compute the equivalent stress ($\sigma_v$)</data>
  <data key="d10">input to,used to compute</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9b2ada8da0499542e52dd4b0404a4d97</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999882</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Principal Stresses" target="Hydrostatic Stress Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The hydrostatic stress tensor ($\sigma$) is computed as the average of the three principal stresses ($\sigma_1 + \sigma_2 + \sigma_3$) divided by 3</data>
