<edge source="Internal Pressure (p)" target="Longitudinal Stress (σ_x)">
  <data key="d8">3.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Longitudinal stress equals p·r/(2t), directly depending on internal pressure, vessel radius, and wall thickness&lt;SEP&gt;The internal pressure induces the longitudinal stress along the axis of the cylinder.&lt;SEP&gt;Internal pressure acting on the end caps induces longitudinal stresses within the vessel wall to maintain force equilibrium.</data>
  <data key="d10">causes,dependency,formula,induces</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-887f545fd528c5ed1b7980ed83618c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-290ff749460960cc500499bfce8172f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14e4d70cf188ab298b97a6d1cf9e80c8</data>
