  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thin-walled Cylindrical Pressure Vessel" target="Circumferential Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The circumferential or hoop stress σφ acts tangent to the circumference of the cylinder's wall, representing one of the two principal stresses resulting from the internal pressure.</data>
  <data key="d10">acts on,stress component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thin-walled Cylindrical Pressure Vessel" target="Wall Thickness">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The wall thickness t is a geometric parameter of the pressure vessel used in establishing force equilibrium to derive the relationship between internal pressure and stresses.</data>
