  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Thin-walled Cylindrical Pressure Vessel" target="Diameter">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The diameter 2r defines the total cross-sectional dimension of the closed cylinder, used in calculating projected areas for force equilibrium analysis.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines,geometric parameter</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7b026fcfc3bb4dcf15d90b692b7902eb</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904247</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Stress Transformation Equations" target="Stationarity Condition For Normal Stresses">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The stress transformation equations are differentiated with respect to φ to derive the stationarity condition for normal stresses.</data>
