</edge>
<edge source="Wall Thickness (t)" target="Thin-walled Pressure Vessel">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The wall thickness t is a defining parameter of thin-walled pressure vessels, assumed to be much smaller than the radius r (t &lt;&lt; r)</data>
  <data key="d10">characteristic,parameter of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904201</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Wall Thickness (t)" target="Vessel Formula">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The wall thickness t is a key parameter in the vessel formula, appearing in the denominator of the ratio r/t</data>
  <data key="d10">parameter in</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-493acae899ca4eaaedf536afa97f481b</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904201</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Wall Thickness (t)" target="Vessel Radius (r)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Wall thickness t is much smaller than vessel radius r (t ≪ r), justifying the thin-wall approximation and the neglect of radial stresses</data>
  <data key="d10">geometric condition,thin-wall approximation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-14e4d70cf188ab298b97a6d1cf9e80c8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904261</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Wall Thickness (t)" target="Maximum Shear Stress (τ_max)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Maximum shear stress is inversely proportional to wall thickness: τ_max = (1/4)·p·r/t</data>
  <data key="d10">formula,inverse dependency</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-14e4d70cf188ab298b97a6d1cf9e80c8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel11_Spannungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784904261</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Trigonometric Identities" target="Stress Transformation Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
