<edge source="Displacement Vector Field Equation" target="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement vector field equation mathematically defines the displacement vector field r(x,y) as a linear combination of Cartesian basis vectors with scalar component functions.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines,mathematical formulation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field Equation" target="Strain Theory">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement vector field equation establishes the kinematic foundation for strain theory.</data>
  <data key="d10">foundation of,kinematic basis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999713</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Two-Dimensional Deformable Body (Scheibe)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement vector field r(x,y) describes the position-dependent deformation of points within a two-dimensional deformable body.</data>
  <data key="d10">applies to,describes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Cartesian Basis Vectors">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement vector field is expressed as a linear combination of Cartesian basis vectors e_x and e_y.</data>
  <data key="d10">decomposed into,expressed using</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Horizontal Displacement Component u(x,y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The scalar function u(x,y) is the horizontal displacement component of the displacement vector field.</data>
  <data key="d10">component of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Vertical Displacement Component v(x,y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The scalar function v(x,y) is the vertical displacement component of the displacement vector field.</data>
  <data key="d10">component of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999712</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Infinitesimal Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The infinitesimal strain tensor is derived through partial differentiation of the displacement field components u(x,y) and v(x,y).</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from,partial differentiation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999713</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Strain Analysis (Verzerrungszustand)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement vector field is central to strain analysis, which addresses how deformation affects side lengths and angles of geometric elements.</data>
  <data key="d10">central to,context of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999713</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Vector Field r(x,y)" target="Gradient of the Displacement Field">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The effect of deformation on side lengths and angles directly connects to the gradient of this displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">connects to,relates to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-873966c9766a35d08748403615a24d1f</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999713</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
