<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Folien 18-20">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The derivation of the relationship between engineering shear strain and tensorial strain is referenced on Folien 18-20.</data>
  <data key="d10">derivation,reference</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7992b48b195836a401d5e2640f4cca33</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999775</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Engineering Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Defines the engineering shear strain component $\gamma_{yz}$ in the y-z plane.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Displacement Field V">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Is mathematically the sum of the partial derivative of the displacement field v with respect to z.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Displacement Field W">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Is mathematically the sum of the partial derivative of the displacement field w with respect to y.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Symmetric Tensor Component">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Equals half of the engineering shear strain $\gamma_{yz}$.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Y-z Plane">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The engineering shear strain component is defined specifically in the y-z plane.</data>
  <data key="d10">defined in</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Undeformed State">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The engineering shear strain reduces the original right angle found in the undeformed state.</data>
  <data key="d10">modifies</data>
