  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999850</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Geometric Kinematic Relationship Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation uses the engineering shear strain (γ) to define the rotation of the deformed diagonal angle.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculates,incorporates</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-55f0f77e6766d722b567e55f8b17701c</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999866</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation γ/2 = ε defines the tensorial relationship involving engineering shear strain γ, establishing its connection to the strain tensor component.</data>
  <data key="d10">definition,tensorial relationship</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Strain Tensor Component">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The relationship γ/2 = ε connects engineering shear strain γ to the strain tensor component ε in the symmetric strain tensor.</data>
  <data key="d10">tensorial relationship</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Symmetric Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The symmetric strain tensor uses half the engineering shear strain (γ/2) as its shear component for coordinate transformation purposes.</data>
  <data key="d10">tensor component,transformation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain" target="Compliance Matrix">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Compliance Matrix in Voigt notation contains the off-diagonal block representing Engineering Shear Strain relations.</data>
