<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="Deformation Gradient Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 1D Taylor expansion acts as the foundational stepping stone that generalizes to the deformation gradient tensor in higher dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d10">generalizes to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afdf7262993e514ad26ba97ab4f2a420</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999719</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="Linearized Infinitesimal Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 1D Taylor expansion concept generalizes to the linearized infinitesimal strain tensor in higher dimensions.</data>
  <data key="d10">generalizes to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-afdf7262993e514ad26ba97ab4f2a420</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999719</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="P'S' Line Segment">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The length of the P'S' segment is calculated using a first-order Taylor series approximation of the displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculation,mathematical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999731</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="Geometric Linear Theory">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Geometric linear theory operates on the assumption that higher-order terms from the Taylor series are negligible.</data>
  <data key="d10">assumption,theoretical basis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="Taylor Series (Taylorreihe)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The first-order Taylor series expansion explicitly applies the abstract mathematical concept of the Taylor series.</data>
  <data key="d10">application,mathematical basis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="First-Order Taylor Series Expansion" target="Small Displacements (kleine Verschiebungen)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The approximation assumes that higher-order terms are negligible, which corresponds to the assumption of small displacements.</data>
  <data key="d10">assumption,simplification</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9f3dea07a2a72e1fd56bdd66b98441fc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999732</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
