<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Deformed State">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The deformed state defines the normal strain through the elongation of the element's sides.</data>
  <data key="d10">causes,defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-77038968edb0f63a8763c004d187bda5</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999737</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Principal Strain Angle">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The principal strain angle is mathematically derived by extremizing the normal strain under coordinate rotation.</data>
  <data key="d10">extremizes,maximizes/minimizes</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-86444d41dc2e58cbf77ceb58838e96c9</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999774</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Poisson Effect">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Normal strain in one direction includes a Poisson coupling term affected by the Poisson effect caused by perpendicular stress.&lt;SEP&gt;The Poisson effect contributes to the normal strain in the x-direction through the term −ν·σ_y in the generalized Hooke's Law equation.</data>
  <data key="d10">affected by,affects,coupled with,lateral contraction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999841</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Principle Of Linear Superposition">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The calculation of normal strain is based on the principle of linear superposition, summing individual stress contributions.</data>
  <data key="d10">basis of,governs</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f0e5bb0f8636d66563ae50a1af38ba22</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999842</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Normal Stress In X-Direction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal stress in the x-direction (σ_x) causes elongation and directly contributes to the normal strain in the x-direction.</data>
  <data key="d10">causes,elongation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999860</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Equation $\varepsilon _ { x } = \frac { 1 } { E } \left( \sigma _ { x } - \nu \cdot \sigma _ { y } \right)$">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation is used to calculate the normal strain in the x-direction based on applied normal stresses and material properties.</data>
  <data key="d10">calculates,defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999860</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Epsilon">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Epsilon is the mathematical variable used to denote normal strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">symbol</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999865</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Tensile Tests">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Normal strain is measured during tensile tests.</data>
  <data key="d10">application,measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999865</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Extensometers">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Normal strain is measured using extensometers.</data>
  <data key="d10">measurement</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-003690f3bd06e7311822e9ac7e4a4393</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999865</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Geometric Kinematic Relationship Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal strain (ε) is a primary variable in the equation, determining the ratio of the deformed diagonal.</data>
  <data key="d10">depends on,incorporates</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-55f0f77e6766d722b567e55f8b17701c</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999866</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Unit Square">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The unit square visually illustrates deformation by showing its corner moving to (1+ε, 1-ε) when acted upon by normal strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">deforms by,illustrates</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-55f0f77e6766d722b567e55f8b17701c</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999866</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain" target="Compliance Matrix Formulation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The compliance form calculates normal strains from normal stresses.</data>
  <data key="d10">Calculates,Outputs</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4640da85a6d88df2121f23eab1d68369</data>
