<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Power Series">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series is explicitly described as a power series (Potenzreihe) in the mathematical formalism.</data>
  <data key="d10">categorized as,type of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999721</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Evaluation/Development Point">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Taylor series expansions are used to approximate arbitrary functions at the evaluation/development point.</data>
  <data key="d10">approximation at</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999722</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="f(y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series is an approximation used to represent the target function f(y).</data>
  <data key="d10">approximation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999723</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="(y - y_0)^n">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series includes (y - y_0)^n as a factor representing the spatial offset from the reference point.</data>
  <data key="d10">component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999723</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="n!">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series includes n! as the normalizing denominator for the series terms.</data>
  <data key="d10">component</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999723</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Infinite Summation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series equation employs the mathematical operation of infinite summation.</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999724</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Higher-order Differentiation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series equation employs the mathematical operation of higher-order differentiation.</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999724</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Factorial Computation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series equation employs the mathematical operation of factorial computation.</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999724</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Polynomial Expansion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series equation employs the mathematical operation of polynomial expansion.</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical operation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e8d2b1a89f6cabb7e72a9e7705515dc</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999724</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Undeformed Reference Configuration">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The reference state serves as the zeroth-order term or anchor for the Taylor series expansion.</data>
  <data key="d10">anchors,basis for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2baa9c55366fde92e0ba418495c7bae0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999725</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Multi-dimensional Strain Analysis">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Taylor series provides the mathematical foundation for progressing to multi-dimensional strain analysis.</data>
  <data key="d10">basis for,foundation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-30b5c4f815450e226a7f0b65824388cf</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999736</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Taylor Series" target="Small Displacement Considerations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Taylor series foundations serve as a starting point that progresses through small displacement considerations.</data>
  <data key="d10">foundation,progresses to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-30b5c4f815450e226a7f0b65824388cf</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999736</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="1-Dimensional Case" target="Multi-Dimensional Case">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The mathematical framework for small displacements in the 1-dimensional case is extended to the multi-dimensional case.</data>
  <data key="d10">extended to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-e4977643a568de41c3595cee58107e8d</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999722</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
