<edge source="Strain Tensor Components" target="Displacement Field v(x, y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement field component v(x, y) is used together with u(x, y) to derive the strain tensor components from the displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">used to derive</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Strain Tensor Components" target="Displacement Field u(x, y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement field components u(x, y) and v(x, y) are used to derive the strain tensor components (εx, εy, γxy) from the displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">used to derive</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Strain Tensor Components" target="Equation PQ: dy = 0">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation PQ: dy = 0 serves as the geometric basis for deriving the strain tensor components (εx, εy, γxy) from the displacement field.</data>
  <data key="d10">derives,geometric basis for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Strain Tensor Components" target="Plane Strain State (EVZ)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The symmetric strain tensor components are used in formulating the plane strain state (EVZ).</data>
  <data key="d10">formulates,used in</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
