<edge source="Equation P Q: d y = 0" target="Normal Strain In X-direction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">By constraining dy = 0, the equation isolates a unidirectional line element along the x-axis, fundamental for analyzing the normal strain in the x-direction.</data>
  <data key="d10">enables,isolates</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2dbfa0f426be66876905754d3b98be</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999734</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Equation P Q: d y = 0" target="Shear Angle Alpha">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The geometric setup defined by the equation provides the basis to analyze the rotation of horizontal lines that contributes to the shear angle alpha.</data>
  <data key="d10">basis for,contributes to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2dbfa0f426be66876905754d3b98be</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999734</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Equation P Q: d y = 0" target="Differential Change In Y-coordinate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation specifies a mathematical mapping condition where the differential change in the y-coordinate along the segment PQ is strictly zero.</data>
  <data key="d10">constrains,specifies</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2dbfa0f426be66876905754d3b98be</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999735</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Equation P Q: d y = 0" target="Horizontal Line Element">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation implies that the line element is oriented perfectly horizontal, creating a horizontal line element.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines,implies</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7a2dbfa0f426be66876905754d3b98be</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999735</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
