<edge source="Equation PQ: dy = 0" target="Line Element PQ">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation PQ: dy = 0 defines the differential line element PQ as oriented parallel to the x-axis with zero differential change in the y-coordinate.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Equation PQ: dy = 0" target="Kinematic Strain-displacement Relations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The geometric constraint of the equation is fundamental in the derivation of the kinematic strain-displacement relations in continuum mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d10">fundamental in derivation of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Line Element PQ" target="Normal Strain εx">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The line element PQ with dy = 0 is used to analyze axial deformation and compute the normal strain εx by examining the change in length after deformation.</data>
  <data key="d10">used to compute</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Line Element PQ" target="Shear Strain γxy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The angular rotation of the line element PQ contributes to the shear strain component α, which is part of the total shear strain γxy = α + β.</data>
  <data key="d10">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Line Element PQ" target="Two-dimensional Continuum">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The differential line element PQ is defined within a two-dimensional continuum.</data>
  <data key="d10">defined within</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Line Element PQ" target="Shear Strain Component α">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The angular rotation of the line element PQ contributes to the shear strain component α.</data>
  <data key="d10">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Line Element PQ" target="Symmetric Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The line element PQ is essential for formulating the symmetric strain tensor used in the plane strain state (EVZ).</data>
  <data key="d10">essential for formulating</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Normal Strain εx" target="Displacement Field u(x, y)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The displacement field component u(x, y) is used to derive the normal strain εx, which equals ∂u/∂x.</data>
  <data key="d10">partial derivative relationship,used to derive</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="Malformed Right Angle Equation (Possible Strain/Geometry Relation) (equation)">
  <data key="d9">Entity Shear Strain γxy belongs to Malformed Right Angle Equation (Possible Strain/Geometry Relation) (equation)&lt;SEP&gt;Entity Shear Strain γxy belongs to Malformed Right Angle Equation (Possible Strain/Geometry Relation) (equation)</data>
  <data key="d10">belongs_to,contained_in,part_of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0646aad7e7ebf134b763f7b7172548fa</data>
  <data key="d8">20.0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999773</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="Shear Strain Component α">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The shear strain component α is part of the total shear strain γxy, such that γxy = α + β.</data>
  <data key="d10">part of,sums to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="Shear Strain Component β">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The shear strain component β is part of the total shear strain γxy, such that γxy = α + β.</data>
  <data key="d10">part of,sums to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-623de8f24fdeee5720ee7518dc88dbb2</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999738</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="Plane Strain State (EVZ)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">EVZ is defined by strain components including the shear strain γxy.</data>
  <data key="d10">defined by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0646aad7e7ebf134b763f7b7172548fa</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999772</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="2D Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 2D strain tensor contains half-shear strains off-diagonal.</data>
  <data key="d10">contains,off-diagonal</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0646aad7e7ebf134b763f7b7172548fa</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999772</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain γxy" target="Principal Strain Directions">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">At principal strain directions, shear strains vanish completely.</data>
  <data key="d10">vanish</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-0646aad7e7ebf134b763f7b7172548fa</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999772</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
