<edge source="Shear Modulus G" target="Poisson's Ratio $\nu$">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The shear modulus G can be mathematically derived from Poisson's ratio $\nu$.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-06ff56a8965495f3a5913389bf912308</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999843</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus G" target="Shear Stress-Shear Strain Constitutive Relation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The constitutive relation uses the shear modulus G as the proportionality constant between shear stress and shear strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">parameter,uses</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-372d45ee57b3e8dd4b75b8ce18594fad</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999847</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus G" target="Torsion Test">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The torsion test is an experimental method used to determine the shear modulus G.</data>
  <data key="d10">determines,experimental</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-372d45ee57b3e8dd4b75b8ce18594fad</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999847</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus G" target="Biaxially Loaded Plate">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The biaxially loaded plate (Scheibe) is used to derive the relationship showing G is derivable from E and ν.</data>
  <data key="d10">derives,relationship</data>
