<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain Equation" target="Spatial Strain Tensor">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Serves as a fundamental kinematic relation for defining the spatial strain tensor components.</data>
  <data key="d10">fundamental relation for</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain Equation" target="Angular Deformations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The given equation represents the direct geometric summation of angular deformations.</data>
  <data key="d10">represents</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Engineering Shear Strain Equation" target="Orthogonal Displacement Components">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">States that the engineering shear strain is the sum of the partial derivatives of the orthogonal displacement components.</data>
  <data key="d10">sums</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999789</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Field V" target="Cartesian Coordinate Z">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The partial derivative $\frac{\partial v}{\partial z}$ represents the rate of change of the displacement field v along the z-axis.</data>
  <data key="d10">rate of change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Displacement Field W" target="Cartesian Coordinate Y">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The partial derivative $\frac{\partial w}{\partial y}$ represents the rate of change of the displacement field w along the y-axis.</data>
  <data key="d10">rate of change</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-aac206a8f9ab7199ba4ae6138d74c7ec</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999788</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
