  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson Effect" target="Normal Stress In Y-Direction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The normal stress in the y-direction (σ_y) induces the Poisson effect, causing lateral contraction or expansion in the x-direction.</data>
  <data key="d10">induces,lateral deformation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999860</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson Effect" target="Normal Strain In Y-direction">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Lateral contraction in the normal strain equation is induced through the Poisson effect.</data>
  <data key="d10">influenced by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999864</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson Effect" target="Material Anisotropy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Material anisotropy of deformation response is demonstrated by the Poisson effect in the strain equation.</data>
  <data key="d10">demonstrated by</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-90b46de3a3db50a2d58052925f2088b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999864</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Poisson Effect" target="Principal Normal Strain">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
