<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Shear Modulus Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Shear Modulus Equation connects the Shear Modulus with Young's Modulus and Poisson's ratio.</data>
  <data key="d10">connects,defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999850</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Torsionsversuch an dünnwandigem Rohr">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Torsionsversuch an dünnwandigem Rohr is an experimental determination used to find the Shear Modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">used to determine</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-40ce366fccc91c18aaa393823e9d843a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999851</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Torsion Testing">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Torsion testing of thin-walled tubes is used to determine the shear modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">determination method</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-2e13c1eccdbc66212f603ee56ccf63b8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999853</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Law Of Elasticity">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Law of Elasticity provides context for the derivation of the relationship between Young's Modulus and Shear Modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">context,derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-a50d9bf013c0aaad48cb4e73c069c450</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999855</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Poisson Effects">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Analysis of coupled deformations and Poisson effects leads to the derivation of the relationship for the shear modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">leads to derivation of</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999858</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="G = E/[2(1+ν)]">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The derived formula mathematically relates the shear modulus to Young's modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">relates to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-7ce85f9ca143dc31ac04d4214fb77217</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999859</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Strain Transformations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Evaluating strain transformations helps to mathematically derive and demonstrate the relationship between Shear Modulus and other elastic properties.</data>
  <data key="d10">derives,interdependence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999860</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Shear Deformations">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Evaluating shear deformations helps to mathematically derive and demonstrate the relationship between Shear Modulus and other elastic properties.</data>
  <data key="d10">derives,interdependence</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-73b7a69e161212c37519887b41d07b9a</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999860</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Modulus" target="Strain Component Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The strain component equation is part of the derivation that establishes the fundamental relationship between Young's Modulus and Shear Modulus.</data>
  <data key="d10">part of derivation for</data>
