  <data key="d13">1784999869</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Strain Tensor Component" target="Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation γ/2 = ε defines the tensorial relationship involving strain tensor component ε, establishing its connection to engineering shear strain.</data>
  <data key="d10">definition,tensorial relationship</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain Equation" target="Elastic Constants Relationship">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The elastic constants relationship G = E/[2(1+ν)] is derived by combining the shear strain equation γ/2 = ε with Hooke's constitutive equation.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination,derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Shear Strain Equation" target="Combined Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The combined shear strain equation is derived by substituting the shear strain equation into Hooke's constitutive equation.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination,result</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Constitutive Equation" target="Elastic Constants Relationship">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The elastic constants relationship G = E/[2(1+ν)] is derived by combining Hooke's constitutive equation ε = σ/E × (1 + ν) with the shear strain equation γ/2 = ε.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination,derivation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hooke's Constitutive Equation" target="Combined Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The combined shear strain equation incorporates Hooke's constitutive law to express shear strain in terms of normal stress and material properties.</data>
  <data key="d10">combination,result</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Elastic Constants Relationship" target="Combined Shear Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The combined shear strain equation leads directly to the derivation of the fundamental relationship between elastic constants.</data>
  <data key="d10">derivation,leads to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-4e81d879c9812c155c5e161dfb7c5f32</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999868</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
