<edge source="Isotropic Material" target="Anisotropic Material">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The 21 independent elastic constants required for a fully anisotropic material are reduced to just 2 for an isotropic material.</data>
  <data key="d10">contrasted with,reduces to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-004e08ca4afebf77525a1d7810f76686</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999869</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Isotropic Material" target="Principal Normal Strain Equation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equation defines the principal normal strain in an isotropic, linearly elastic material.</data>
  <data key="d10">defines</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-5804dc5da5931340fcffd232bf52ac41</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
