<edge source="Distortion Energy Hypothesis" target="Distortion Energy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Per the distortion energy hypothesis, plastic deformation and yielding are governed solely by the distortion energy U_f.</data>
  <data key="d10">governs,plastic deformation</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f89ffe71648491b9b2c362db33adecfd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortion Energy Hypothesis" target="Plastic Deformation">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">According to the distortion energy hypothesis, plastic deformation is governed solely by the energy required to change the material's shape.</data>
  <data key="d10">governs</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f89ffe71648491b9b2c362db33adecfd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortion Energy Hypothesis" target="Distortional Energy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The distortion energy hypothesis (Gestaltänderungsenergie) is derived based on the concept that distortional energy governs plastic yielding in materials.</data>
  <data key="d10">theoretical basis</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortion Energy Hypothesis" target="Von Mises Equivalent Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The Von Mises Equivalent Stress is derived from the Distortion Energy Hypothesis by equating the distortion energy of a general 3D stress state with that of a uniaxial tensile stress state</data>
  <data key="d10">based on,derived from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-9b2ada8da0499542e52dd4b0404a4d97</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999882</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
