</edge>
<edge source="Uniaxial Tensile Test" target="Von Mises Yield Criterion">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The von Mises yield criterion mathematically equates the distortion energy of a complex 3D stress state to that of a simple uniaxial tensile test.</data>
  <data key="d10">Mathematical Comparison</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7593a3adc530882efa765d69efe9aa0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999882</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Uniaxial Tensile Test" target="Equivalent Stress ($\sigma_v$)">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The equivalent stress is compared to known material limits from a uniaxial tensile test to predict whether a material will yield.</data>
  <data key="d10">Material Yield Prediction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-b7593a3adc530882efa765d69efe9aa0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
