<edge source="Total Internal Strain Energy" target="Substitution Von Epsilon 1, Epsilon 2 Und Epsilon 3">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total internal strain energy is expressed entirely in terms of principal stresses through the substitution of strain components.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived by,expressed via</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Total Internal Strain Energy" target="Distortional Energy">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total internal strain energy U is decomposed into the distortional energy U_f and the hydrostatic energy component U_h.&lt;SEP&gt;The total internal strain energy U is decomposed into distortional energy (causing shape changes and plastic yielding) and hydrostatic energy (causing volumetric changes).</data>
  <data key="d10">contains,decomposed into,decomposition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Total Internal Strain Energy" target="Hydrostatic Strain Energy Density">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total internal strain energy U is decomposed into distortional energy and hydrostatic energy, where the hydrostatic portion corresponds to U_h representing purely volumetric energy.</data>
  <data key="d10">decomposition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Total Internal Strain Energy" target="Hydrostatic Energy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total internal strain energy U is decomposed into distortional energy and hydrostatic energy components.</data>
  <data key="d10">decomposition</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortional Energy" target="Hydrostatic Energy Component">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Distortional energy U_f is obtained by subtracting the hydrostatic energy component U_h from the total internal strain energy U.</data>
  <data key="d10">complementary,subtracted from</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-1a375818483fffe9d5cdc368f45b60b8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortional Energy" target="Hydrostatic Strain Energy Density">
  <data key="d8">2.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The effective distortion energy U_f is calculated by subtracting the hydrostatic strain energy density U_h from the total internal strain energy U (U_f = U - U_h).&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrostatic strain energy density is subtracted from total strain energy to isolate the distortional energy.</data>
  <data key="d10">mathematical_mechanism,subtracted_to_isolate,subtraction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-6b27cb9b72646a5e65e44fef0102a7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c347d0d02f605dcaeeba6088d212ddc8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Distortional Energy" target="Von Mises Equivalent Stress">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">Distortional energy is set equal to the energy of a uniaxial tensile test to mathematically derive the von Mises equivalent stress.</data>
  <data key="d10">derivation_step,equated_to</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-c347d0d02f605dcaeeba6088d212ddc8</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999881</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Energy Component" target="Strain Energy Density">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The total strain energy density U is decomposed into a volumetric (hydrostatic) component U_h as part of the strength hypotheses framework.</data>
  <data key="d10">decomposed into</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f89ffe71648491b9b2c362db33adecfd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Hydrostatic Energy Component" target="Distortion Energy">
  <data key="d8">1.0</data>
  <data key="d9">The distortion energy U_f is derived by subtracting the hydrostatic portion U_h from the total strain energy U.</data>
  <data key="d10">derived from,subtraction</data>
  <data key="d11">chunk-f89ffe71648491b9b2c362db33adecfd</data>
  <data key="d12">Kapitel12_Verzerrungszustand.pdf</data>
  <data key="d13">1784999879</data>
  <data key="d14"></data>
</edge>
